chapter_group.14B07D44F866BE42.title: "Mission Control: Progress Tracker"
	chapter_group.1602D78D572DB7CA.title: "Main Route 3/5: Industrial Systems"
	chapter_group.163788D5CCF4125E.title: "Main Route 1/5: Orientation"
	chapter_group.1FA6C12B57D8715D.title: "Main Route 5/5: Interplanetary Industry"
	chapter_group.381BEBAB6F4DDA31.title: "Main Route 2/5: Factory Foundations"
	chapter_group.3C2D009B803A50D5.title: "Main Route 4/5: Space Program"
	chapter_group.638D7E94571D529E.title: "Optional Systems and Worldbuilding"
	chapter_group.6FE76C5D41AD6C79.title: "Reference and Mastery"
	quest.0055F6CC13881FB3.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft at least one Printed Circuit Board."
		"Why this matters: This is the reward for understanding pressure processing and technical staging. It signals that your base can now produce genuinely advanced components."
		"Step by step: Work through the full chain calmly. If a step fails, verify the previous intermediate was the exact expected item."
		"Common mistake: Guessing substitutes for intermediate items causes most confusion here."
	]
	quest.0055F6CC13881FB3.quest_subtitle: "A true high-tech milestone."
	quest.0055F6CC13881FB3.title: "Make a Printed Circuit Board"
	quest.008FA38B5E7207A4.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Create a simple network with an Energy Cable and Energy Cell."
		"Why this matters: Energy buffers smooth out power spikes and make machines easier to diagnose. If the cell fills, generation works. If it drains, demand is higher than supply."
		"Step by step: Craft basic cable and a basic cell, connect your generator, and watch energy move."
		"Common mistake: Running every machine directly from generators makes troubleshooting much harder."
	]
	quest.008FA38B5E7207A4.quest_subtitle: "Generator, cable, buffer."
	quest.008FA38B5E7207A4.title: "Build the smallest useful grid"
	quest.009D5F2EA7E7D8AC.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Autocrafter."
		"Why this matters: The Autocrafter holds patterns and performs crafting jobs when the network receives a request. It is the engine behind recipe automation."
		"Step by step: Place it connected to the Refined Storage network and insert one simple pattern first."
		"Common mistake: A Pattern Grid alone does not craft anything. It only encodes instructions."
	]
	quest.009D5F2EA7E7D8AC.quest_subtitle: "The network needs a place to execute patterns."
	quest.009D5F2EA7E7D8AC.title: "Build the Autocrafter"
	quest.00BBA65077B28051.quest_desc: [
		"Industrial Foregoing excels at practical automation: farming, animals, mob byproducts, fluids, and processing frameworks that reduce repeated manual chores."
		"This chapter is optional for the main space route, but it makes long-running worlds more comfortable and can support self-sufficient outposts."
		"Use it where it removes a genuine pain point."
		"Begin with one compact loop whose benefit is obvious, such as crops, animals, or mob byproducts. Optional automation should earn its footprint."
	]
	quest.00BBA65077B28051.quest_subtitle: "Automate living-world chores where it helps."
	quest.00BBA65077B28051.title: "Optional: resource automation through Industrial Foregoing"
	quest.01375AEE12275C25.quest_desc: [
		"Take your prepared rocket on its first true mission. This is the first point where the pack asks you to act in the world rather than just craft components."
		"For this pack, treat the Moon as the first planned destination. Keep the trip focused: land safely, observe the environment, gather the Moon materials requested below, and return or establish a safe anchor."
		"Do not treat the first mission as a blind speedrun."
		"On arrival, prioritize orientation, survival, and return confidence over greedy mining. The first expedition teaches the rhythm of safe planetary travel."
	]
	quest.01375AEE12275C25.quest_subtitle: "The industrial arc reaches another world."
	quest.01375AEE12275C25.title: "Launch and travel beyond Earth"
	quest.01A493C0165ECCE4.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a 1M MEGA Item Storage Cell."
		"Why this matters: MEGA Cells expands AE2 with a dedicated high-capacity progression instead of leaving the optional branch feeling thin beside the main Refined Storage route."
		"Step by step: Add it only after you understand ordinary AE2 storage cells, then decide which item classes belong in giant cells and which deserve external handling."
		"Common mistake: Bigger cells do not replace thoughtful type management."
	]
	quest.01A493C0165ECCE4.quest_subtitle: "The expert storage branch gains real endgame capacity."
	quest.01A493C0165ECCE4.title: "Build a MEGA 1M item cell"
	quest.01E227ABF3087E46.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build a modest resource buffer before starting Create and Mekanism."
		"Why this matters: This pack uses traditional metals alongside modded materials. Iron and copper build machines, redstone enables control, and osmium opens Mekanism."
		"Step by step: Mine until you can smelt at least a small reserve of iron, copper, and osmium. Redstone becomes important shortly after."
		"Common mistake: Starting multiple tech mods with only a few ingots causes stop-and-go crafting."
	]
	quest.01E227ABF3087E46.quest_subtitle: "Iron, copper, redstone, and osmium define the early climb."
	quest.01E227ABF3087E46.title: "Collect the ores that matter"
	quest.01F389BA19A8EAF1.quest_desc: [
		"Look at the Pressure Gauge. If pressure is too low, the system lacks compression or air is being consumed faster than produced. If pressure is climbing beyond safe operation, stop expanding blindly and check the network design."
		"Confirm that the machine actually accepts pressure from the connected side and that required items are present."
		"Never treat pressure as invisible background magic."
		"A gauge plus a calm checklist beats random rebuilding. Pressure systems become safe when every symptom has an observable cause."
	]
	quest.01F389BA19A8EAF1.quest_subtitle: "Pressure is a measured system."
	quest.01F389BA19A8EAF1.title: "When PneumaticCraft feels dangerous or inactive"
	quest.02007FB6E088933A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce fuel and capture a bucket of it."
		"Why this matters: A bucket is a small milestone, but it proves every earlier assumption: source, refinery, recipe, and output all work."
		"Step by step: Run the refinery until you have fuel available, then obtain one Fuel Bucket and keep it in the launch staging area."
		"Common mistake: Do not try to diagnose launch issues before confirming that your fuel chain can produce actual fuel."
	]
	quest.02007FB6E088933A.quest_subtitle: "Prove the fuel chain works."
	quest.02007FB6E088933A.title: "Create the first Fuel Bucket"
	quest.020D3CB4A3062BCA.quest_desc: [
		"Early FE power proved the concept. Midgame power must absorb wider automation, longer machine runs, and off-world preparation without constant babysitting."
		"This chapter expands capacity, transmission, and thoughtful power placement. The goal is stability, not a single oversized generator built for screenshots."
		"Watch production and storage together. A large empty energy cell is not a power solution."
		"A stable grid is one whose behavior you can predict under load. Watch generation, storage, and demand before assuming bigger machines are the answer."
	]
	quest.020D3CB4A3062BCA.quest_subtitle: "Your power grid must support factories and launch support."
	quest.020D3CB4A3062BCA.title: "Energy becomes infrastructure"
	quest.022A887A89745303.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Stove."
		"Why this matters: The stove helps establish a recognizable kitchen and makes your base feel more complete. This is especially welcome in worlds that last through many space missions."
		"Step by step: Place it near storage for ingredients or beside a planned cooking pot."
		"Common mistake: A kitchen hidden among chemical machines misses the point of comfort-building."
	]
	quest.022A887A89745303.quest_subtitle: "Food deserves a dedicated cooking space."
	quest.022A887A89745303.title: "Add a Stove"
	quest.02CA85258118904C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Encased Fan and learn the idea of bulk processing."
		"Why this matters: Create can wash, haunt, smoke, or blast items by blowing air through the correct block. This is a major early-game efficiency jump."
		"Step by step: Start with a fan and inspect its JEI uses. Build a short test area where the fan can blow through the required block safely."
		"Common mistake: The fan direction matters. If particles move the wrong way, the recipe will not happen."
	]
	quest.02CA85258118904C.quest_subtitle: "Fans turn environmental blocks into recipes."
	quest.02CA85258118904C.title: "Introduce bulk processing"
	quest.02F5005587813C71.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an AE2 Crafting Terminal."
		"Why this matters: This is the user-facing heart of the optional network. It gives the system a reason to exist in daily play rather than being a collection of impressive blocks."
		"Step by step: Connect it properly and confirm the network recognizes it."
		"Common mistake: A powered-looking block is not always connected to the AE2 network in the correct way."
	]
	quest.02F5005587813C71.quest_subtitle: "Access and crafting belong together."
	quest.02F5005587813C71.title: "Add a Crafting Terminal"
	quest.03077158E81338BF.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Phantom Itemface."
		"Why this matters: Phantom systems reward players who like compact rooms, hidden interfaces, and cleaner machine access."
		"Use them sparingly at first so the item path stays understandable."
		"Build a tiny demonstration that solves one clear problem, such as remote access to a concealed buffer or a cleaner machine-wall interface."
		"Remote access is strongest when it reduces clutter without hiding the system's purpose from the player."
	]
	quest.03077158E81338BF.quest_subtitle: "Remote access is powerful when the layout remains readable."
	quest.03077158E81338BF.title: "Test Phantom routing"
	quest.03B7D9AD5F6FA454.quest_desc: [
		"Pick a component you genuinely repeat in Stellar Foundry: a storage part, a machine subcomponent, or a crafting ingredient from an earlier chapter."
		"Encode the pattern path and prove the network can produce it when asked. This turns autocrafting from a demo into a permanent quality-of-life improvement."
		"Keep the first real autocraft modest. Reliability is more valuable than ambition here."
		"Choose something you actually craft repeatedly in this pack. Autocrafting feels powerful only when it removes a real recurring interruption."
	]
	quest.03B7D9AD5F6FA454.quest_subtitle: "Make the lesson matter to this pack."
	quest.03B7D9AD5F6FA454.title: "Autocraft one recurring technical component"
	quest.045E6A317479CA79.quest_desc: [
		"Stellar Foundry is a technical pack, but long projects feel better when the base is hospitable: good food, clear rooms, safe storage for valuables, and small details that turn a machine hub into a home."
		"This chapter is optional and intentionally light. It rewards a world that is satisfying to inhabit between major progression pushes."
		"A pleasant base increases the chance that players stay for the long arc."
		"Slice and Dice, Torchmaster, and Trash Cans round out the comfort layer with cleaner kitchens, safer bases, and less inventory friction."
	]
	quest.045E6A317479CA79.quest_subtitle: "Comfort systems support long-term play."
	quest.045E6A317479CA79.title: "Optional: make the industrial world pleasant to live in"
	quest.053A95E287A2EE02.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Warp Stone and connect your important places conceptually."
		"Why this matters: A strong world has clear routes: main base, mine, launch site, colony access, and utility zones. Travel tools should support that clarity."
		"Step by step: Use the Warp Stone or existing Waystones to make your world easier to navigate without erasing the feeling of location."
		"Common mistake: Fast travel is most useful when destinations are named and built intentionally."
	]
	quest.053A95E287A2EE02.quest_subtitle: "Paths, rooms, and waystones are quality of life."
	quest.053A95E287A2EE02.title: "Add practical travel infrastructure"
	quest.058D6673A7642ADB.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the table that introduces this addon’s rocket workflow."
		"Why this matters: The Engineering Table gives this route its own identity. It makes the rocket feel designed rather than simply crafted."
		"Step by step: Craft the table, place it near a Create-oriented engineering area, and inspect its use before mass-producing components."
		"Common mistake: Placing new systems in random corners makes the addon feel more confusing than it is."
	]
	quest.058D6673A7642ADB.quest_subtitle: "Design begins at a dedicated workstation."
	quest.058D6673A7642ADB.title: "Craft the Rocket Engineering Table"
	quest.05C869FB382418F2.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Alternator."
		"Why this matters: The Alternator is the central bridge from Create motion into FE production and lets mechanical players power nearby systems elegantly."
		"Test it with a modest kinetic setup before expanding."
		"Measure whether the mechanical input is strong and steady enough for the desired electrical role before calling the setup complete."
		"It should be understandable why this machine produces FE in your factory and what part of the Create system enables it."
	]
	quest.05C869FB382418F2.quest_subtitle: "Rotation now has a power-grid outlet."
	quest.05C869FB382418F2.title: "Generate FE with an Alternator"
	quest.05D5885DB7DD55A6.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Blast Brick."
		"Why this matters: The Blast Furnace theme fits Stellar Foundry’s heavy-industry layer and rewards players who enjoy slower, physical industrial infrastructure."
		"Step by step: Gather the materials, craft the bricks, and place them only after checking the intended multiblock pattern."
		"Common mistake: A multiblock copied from memory with one wrong block will not form."
	]
	quest.05D5885DB7DD55A6.quest_subtitle: "Steel-era industry looks substantial."
	quest.05D5885DB7DD55A6.title: "Prepare Blast Furnace bricks"
	quest.069412643812B138.quest_desc: [
		"Stellar Foundry treats spaceflight as the result of earlier industry. You now have mechanical processing, FE power, components, storage, logistics, and pressure systems."
		"The next quests create a small set of pack-specific bridge items. They do not replace the space mod. They connect your existing factory to it."
		"If a bridge recipe feels expensive, that is a signal to improve the production chain behind it."
		"Iron Jetpacks can serve as a practical mobility helper while building launch infrastructure and working around tall space-program structures."
	]
	quest.069412643812B138.quest_subtitle: "This is where the factory starts pointing upward."
	quest.069412643812B138.title: "Open the space program"
	quest.06E0D3F19338597C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Crafting Grid after the basic network works."
		"Why this matters: This block transforms the network from a chest search tool into your daily crafting station. It is one of the biggest comfort upgrades in the pack."
		"Step by step: Replace or complement the regular Grid and start using the network as your main recipe staging area."
		"Common mistake: Do not discard the lesson of physical buffers. Digital access and factory logistics serve different roles."
	]
	quest.06E0D3F19338597C.quest_subtitle: "Search and craft in one place."
	quest.06E0D3F19338597C.title: "Upgrade to a Crafting Grid"
	quest.070460A49959AE31.quest_desc: [
		"The next chapters use advanced components from your existing factories, including PneumaticCraft materials. This is intentional: rockets should be the result of an industrial ecosystem."
		"Before moving on, ensure your compressor, gauges, and chamber are understood rather than merely placed."
		"A space program built on systems you can maintain is far more satisfying than a rushed launch."
		"If you cannot explain where air is produced, where it is consumed, and which gauge confirms that, this is the perfect moment to pause and tidy the system."
	]
	quest.070460A49959AE31.quest_subtitle: "You are ready for space-program bridge recipes."
	quest.070460A49959AE31.title: "Pressure systems checkpoint"
	quest.0791788D883583F4.quest_desc: [
		"Complete the charter when your world has: a stable workshop-to-factory progression, digital storage, repeatable launch support, at least one real colony, advanced industrial components, the crafted Interplanetary Industry Charter, and a clear strategy for future missions."
		"This is the intended conclusion of the main progression. From here, mastery challenges and optional systems can keep the world alive for as long as you like."
		"You did not simply craft a rocket. You built the civilization that can keep launching."
		"Claim it when the world could plausibly support many future launches without losing its structure. The Charter rewards a system, not a speedrun."
	]
	quest.0791788D883583F4.quest_subtitle: "The world has become a true industrial space program."
	quest.0791788D883583F4.title: "Stellar Foundry Charter"
	quest.07ED9D6C5A1242C1.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Building Gadget."
		"Why this matters: Industrial bases and launch sites benefit from larger floors, walls, and repeated patterns. The gadget reduces repetitive placement work."
		"Step by step: Craft it, test it on a small harmless construction patch, and learn the tool before using it on your main base."
		"Common mistake: Large-area tools reward previewing. Careless clicks can produce large cleanup jobs."
	]
	quest.07ED9D6C5A1242C1.quest_subtitle: "Large projects should be enjoyable, not repetitive."
	quest.07ED9D6C5A1242C1.title: "Use a Building Gadget"
	quest.08084BB7B7F3D735.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Empowerer."
		"Why this matters: Empowered crystals are the capstone material line of this optional branch and create a satisfying mini-progression."
		"Build the station in a symmetrical, readable work area."
		"Gather the supporting pieces and reserve a symmetrical footprint before you commit to placement. The Empowerer is easiest to read when it looks deliberate."
		"A clean Empowerer area prevents later confusion about which ingredients belong where and makes advanced material crafting feel ceremonial in the best way."
	]
	quest.08084BB7B7F3D735.quest_subtitle: "A compact multiblock-like ritual for materials, not magic."
	quest.08084BB7B7F3D735.title: "Prepare the Empowerer"
	quest.08BFA79E73BFD670.quest_desc: [
		"Stellar Foundry is prepared for a smoother beginner experience: shader support is planned through Iris + Sodium in the CurseForge release, while Fast Leaf Decay removes lingering tree canopies automatically."
		"Jade Addons improves in-world information for modded blocks, and Shulker Box Tooltip helps you inspect container contents without opening every box."
		"Shaders remain optional. If performance matters more than visuals, leave them disabled and use the pack normally."
		"Treat visuals as optional and information tools as practical. A polished pack should stay comfortable both for players chasing beauty and players chasing stability."
	]
	quest.08BFA79E73BFD670.quest_subtitle: "Optional visuals, clearer information, less friction."
	quest.08BFA79E73BFD670.title: "Quality-of-Life and Shader Notes"
	quest.08DD30DC9ED14128.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Wireless Universal Terminal from AE2 Wireless Terminals."
		"Why this matters: AE2 is intentionally the more structured optional storage route. Wireless terminal access rewards that planning by making a mature network feel powerful during building and travel."
		"Step by step: Craft the terminal only after the wired network is understandable. Convenience should grow from mastery."
		"Common mistake: Wireless access does not fix an AE2 network whose power, channels, or storage design is unclear."
	]
	quest.08DD30DC9ED14128.quest_subtitle: "The optional expert network becomes practical in the field."
	quest.08DD30DC9ED14128.title: "Add a Wireless Universal Terminal"
	quest.08FD3C8E0622336C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Reserve a dedicated launch zone near, but not inside, your main factory."
		"Why this matters: Rockets and launch-support blocks deserve a readable area. A clear platform makes progression feel intentional and keeps the base easier to expand."
		"Step by step: Flatten or construct a medium platform, provide access paths, and leave room for future fuel, storage, and safety blocks."
		"Common mistake: A rocket pad squeezed between machines looks improvised and makes future upgrades awkward."
	]
	quest.08FD3C8E0622336C.quest_subtitle: "Do not put critical infrastructure in the middle of your workshop."
	quest.08FD3C8E0622336C.title: "Choose the first launch location"
	quest.090D9424577407E2.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Flux Point."
		"Why this matters: The Point is the output side of wireless FE. It is the natural partner for launchpads, distant workshops, and colonies that need utility power without kilometer-long cable paths."
		"Step by step: Place one at a remote consumer and decide whether the site also needs local storage."
		"Common mistake: Wireless FE is clean only when each endpoint still has a clear purpose."
	]
	quest.090D9424577407E2.quest_subtitle: "Deliver energy where the mission needs it."
	quest.090D9424577407E2.title: "Build a Flux Point"
	quest.0954FD1F905855D1.quest_desc: [
		"Bring together all four Mission Control seals. This final tracker quest is intentionally separate from the main story ending: it rewards the player who collected and claimed the full milestone arc."
		"The completion seal is a trophy item for long worlds, archive rooms, and screenshots of a finished Stellar Foundry run. It also activates the rare Foundry Overdrive Field Protocol."
		"It is safe to leave this final tracker until the very end. Mission Control should celebrate completion, not pressure the route unnaturally."
		"If one seal is missing, revisit the milestone tier above rather than guessing. The tracker is designed to point back to the exact unfinished era."
	]
	quest.0954FD1F905855D1.quest_subtitle: "All four reward tiers collected."
	quest.0954FD1F905855D1.title: "Mission Control Complete"
	quest.0959E7CEB451F6A2.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Martian Reactor Brief."
		"Why this matters: Plutonium and Tharsite now point toward a deliberate industrial study instead of being only trophies in storage."
		"The brief represents a Mars-focused processing or power project you may later build into a real outpost."
		"Keep one copy near your Mars staging area or reactor notes. The brief should feel like a design document inside your world, not only a recipe result."
	]
	quest.0959E7CEB451F6A2.quest_subtitle: "Mars should justify a technical return trip."
	quest.0959E7CEB451F6A2.title: "Compile a Martian Reactor Brief"
	quest.09D8CC4FE47FA0ED.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Energy Cube as a machine-room buffer."
		"Why this matters: Mekanism machines can draw power at awkward moments. A visible energy buffer tells you whether the issue is production, cabling, or machine setup."
		"Step by step: Connect the cube into the FE system, then power at least one Mekanism machine from it."
		"Common mistake: If every machine runs directly from a generator, debugging power becomes guesswork."
	]
	quest.09D8CC4FE47FA0ED.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism should not depend on loose generator wiring."
	quest.09D8CC4FE47FA0ED.title: "Create an Energy Cube"
	quest.0A42148061052EBC.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a Starter Battery and use it as a quick test of your energy system. Charge it, move it, and verify that your network is producing usable FE."
		"From now on, Mekanism and other machines will expect energy. If this chapter felt shaky, fix the layout before advancing."
		"A reliable early grid is more valuable than rushing to an impressive machine that stays unpowered."
		"If the battery behaves unpredictably, trace the system from generator to cable to buffer to consumer. Good power troubleshooting follows the path of the energy."
	]
	quest.0A42148061052EBC.quest_subtitle: "Your next machines need a stable FE source."
	quest.0A42148061052EBC.title: "Power reliability checkpoint"
	quest.0AAF6CB5314ED4EE.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Cooking Pot."
		"Why this matters: The pot expands your food options and gives a clear purpose to a small kitchen. Better food is not mandatory for rockets, but it improves the pace of a long modpack."
		"Step by step: Place it above suitable heat, inspect its recipes, and choose one meal to make in your world."
		"Common mistake: Ignoring the mod entirely leaves a quality-of-life system unused."
	]
	quest.0AAF6CB5314ED4EE.quest_subtitle: "Better meals for long construction sessions."
	quest.0AAF6CB5314ED4EE.title: "Cook with a Cooking Pot"
	quest.0B0717FAAA758910.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the basic compressor that creates compressed air."
		"Why this matters: Without air pressure, PneumaticCraft devices cannot operate. The compressor is to pressure what a generator is to FE."
		"Step by step: Place it in a visible area with room for tubes and gauges. Prepare to monitor the network, not just power it blindly."
		"Common mistake: A hidden compressor makes it easy to miss dangerous or empty pressure conditions."
	]
	quest.0B0717FAAA758910.quest_subtitle: "The heart of the pressure network."
	quest.0B0717FAAA758910.title: "Build an Air Compressor"
	quest.0B4E2BF9CB118EB2.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Set up the basic tools for repeated crafting."
		"Why this matters: Even in a technology pack, the first hour is smoother when crafting, smelting, and storage are placed in one compact area."
		"Step by step: Place a crafting table, at least two furnaces, and a few starter chests. Keep a free wall or floor section for your first modded machines."
		"Common mistake: Spreading starter blocks randomly makes later automation routes messy."
	]
	quest.0B4E2BF9CB118EB2.quest_subtitle: "Keep your base workflow simple."
	quest.0B4E2BF9CB118EB2.title: "Craft a proper crafting station"
	quest.0B69141FAEDAFA16.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build a small rotation line from the Water Wheel."
		"Why this matters: Shafts carry rotation straight. Cogwheels redirect or mesh networks. Learn this visually now because nearly every later Create machine depends on it."
		"Step by step: Craft shafts and cogwheels, then connect them to the wheel until you can see rotation travelling across the build."
		"Common mistake: A machine touching a shaft visually may still be unconnected if the orientation is wrong."
	]
	quest.0B69141FAEDAFA16.quest_subtitle: "Shafts are Create wiring."
	quest.0B69141FAEDAFA16.title: "Transmit motion with shafts"
	quest.0B77CD8BC983B09A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the first stable rotational source."
		"Why this matters: A Water Wheel is simple, passive, and forgiving. It gives enough capacity to learn transmission and power your first press or mixer."
		"Step by step: Craft the Water Wheel and place it in a flow arrangement that actually turns it. Watch the animation to confirm it works."
		"Common mistake: A motionless wheel is not decorative power. It must rotate."
	]
	quest.0B77CD8BC983B09A.quest_subtitle: "Start with a Water Wheel."
	quest.0B77CD8BC983B09A.title: "Create rotational power"
	quest.0B7AFB97FF561619.quest_desc: [
		"Mission Control is the permanent overview for the pack's most important milestone patches. It exists so progress does not disappear into separate chapters."
		"Claim the Logbook, then return here whenever you want to see which major era is complete, which reward tier is next, and which Field Protocol seals you can activate."
		"The four main reward tiers are Foundations, Industrial Systems, Spaceflight, and Interplanetary Industry."
		"Return here after major chapters instead of treating this as a single early stop. Mission Control is meant to summarize a living playthrough."
	]
	quest.0B7AFB97FF561619.quest_subtitle: "One chapter that tells you how far the factory has come."
	quest.0B7AFB97FF561619.title: "Open Mission Control"
	quest.0D383107CBCF9503.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build a small storage system for colony operations."
		"Why this matters: Mining samples, spare food, construction blocks, and atmospheric supplies should have predictable homes. This is especially important when returning after hours of overworld work."
		"Step by step: Craft a Sophisticated Storage Controller or an equivalent local storage focal point and use it in the colony plan."
		"Common mistake: A pile of temporary chests is not a colony storage system."
	]
	quest.0D383107CBCF9503.quest_subtitle: "Colonies need flow, not only chests."
	quest.0D383107CBCF9503.title: "Provide local storage and transport"
	quest.0D960380C2DD87EC.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Animal Rancher."
		"Why this matters: This block demonstrates that automation can interact with entities and farms in more nuanced ways than simple crop harvesting."
		"Step by step: Inspect its behavior, decide whether it suits your world, and integrate it only if it improves a resource loop you care about."
		"Common mistake: Adding machines because they exist, rather than because they solve a problem, creates clutter."
	]
	quest.0D960380C2DD87EC.quest_subtitle: "Use the right machine for the right ethical task."
	quest.0D960380C2DD87EC.title: "Explore animal resource automation"
	quest.0DAE16F92BCFBFDB.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft or prepare the Metal Press block route."
		"Why this matters: The Metal Press is a classic Immersive Engineering machine and a satisfying build for players who enjoy tangible factory hardware."
		"Step by step: Use the manual to confirm its structure and role before integrating it beside Create or Mekanism setups."
		"Common mistake: Do not force every mod into one processing line. Use machines where they add value or character."
	]
	quest.0DAE16F92BCFBFDB.quest_subtitle: "Industrial machinery can be part of your visual factory identity."
	quest.0DAE16F92BCFBFDB.title: "Meet the Metal Press"
	quest.0E75AAD62E72A206.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Small Connector."
		"Why this matters: Connectors make the network legible and help electrical builds feel like designed rooms rather than a pile of cables."
		"Use them where machine boundaries are clear."
		"Plan where wires enter and leave a machine zone before scattering connectors. Good electrical layouts have intentional boundaries."
		"Connector placement is visual communication: it should explain the path of the network, not obscure it."
	]
	quest.0E75AAD62E72A206.quest_subtitle: "Good connections are part of good workshop design."
	quest.0E75AAD62E72A206.title: "Add a Connector"
	quest.0EAC2BDA823E37E3.quest_desc: [
		"This tier binds together the long endgame arc: deeper destinations, planetary industry projects, permanent colonies, and the Stellar Foundry Charter."
		"Why this matters: the modpack should leave a world behind, not a pile of completed recipes. This tier represents that world-scale achievement."
		"Reward: an interplanetary seal, XP, and an advanced deposit upgrade for late-game logistics comfort. Its Field Protocol supports remote construction work."
		"The reward is deliberately comfort-focused because the achievement itself is already enormous: a world-scale industry that spans locations."
	]
	quest.0EAC2BDA823E37E3.quest_subtitle: "A factory network that now spans worlds."
	quest.0EAC2BDA823E37E3.title: "Milestone Tier IV: Interplanetary Industry"
	quest.11533E9175FF8477.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Fuel Refinery."
		"Why this matters: The refinery is a perfect example of why the pack prioritizes industrial preparation. It turns spaceflight into a repeatable supply chain."
		"Step by step: Place it near your launch support area or in a connected fuel-processing zone. Keep fluid routing space available."
		"Common mistake: Burying fuel machines inside general crafting clutter makes refills and upgrades annoying."
	]
	quest.11533E9175FF8477.quest_subtitle: "Raw oil becomes launch fuel through infrastructure."
	quest.11533E9175FF8477.title: "Build a Fuel Refinery"
	quest.1163FAB98071908E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Energizer."
		"Why this matters: Actually Additions becomes more readable when item charging is handled near the machines that consume that charge."
		"Keep the Energizer close to a small buffer or power handoff."
		"Route power cleanly enough that a new player could identify where charge enters and where charged items belong."
		"This is a small-scale energy lesson: local convenience systems should still obey the same clarity rules as major factory infrastructure."
	]
	quest.1163FAB98071908E.quest_subtitle: "Charged tools belong near the workbench that uses them."
	quest.1163FAB98071908E.title: "Store and move energy locally"
	quest.117E2FA520E68F50.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Starter Furnator as your first simple FE generator."
		"Why this matters: The goal is not endgame power. The goal is to run the first energy recipes and teach the layout of generator, cable, storage, and machine."
		"Step by step: Place the Furnator where it can be fueled easily. Route energy to the Rod or an Energy Cell."
		"Common mistake: A generator sitting beside a machine does not always connect the way you imagine. Check sides and cables."
	]
	quest.117E2FA520E68F50.quest_subtitle: "Use a Furnator to begin."
	quest.117E2FA520E68F50.title: "Generate starter energy"
	quest.1267F5A3017E4621.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a small reserve of Pressure Sealant."
		"Why this matters: This component turns PneumaticCraft progress into a clear space-program payoff. It represents sealing, insulation, and preparation for dangerous environments."
		"Step by step: Make at least four pieces. Store them with advanced mission components rather than ordinary raw materials."
		"Common mistake: Crafting exactly one for a recipe creates a needless stop later."
	]
	quest.1267F5A3017E4621.quest_subtitle: "Spaceflight needs industrial sealing materials."
	quest.1267F5A3017E4621.title: "Pressure Sealant belongs in the launch chain"
	quest.129C85B3E8DD7012.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Autocrafting Monitor."
		"Why this matters: Complex jobs can take time or wait on missing ingredients. A monitor tells you what the network is doing and where a job stopped."
		"Step by step: Place the monitor where you plan future factory work and open it during a request."
		"Common mistake: Without monitoring, it is easy to assume the system is broken when it is simply missing one input."
	]
	quest.129C85B3E8DD7012.quest_subtitle: "Every queue deserves visibility."
	quest.129C85B3E8DD7012.title: "Monitor crafting jobs"
	quest.12D1442268511209.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Autocrafter Manager."
		"Why this matters: As pattern counts grow, management becomes a real concern. The manager gives you a central view instead of forcing you to hunt through each block."
		"Step by step: Use it to review where patterns live and decide whether your recipe organization makes sense."
		"Common mistake: Autocrafting systems become frustrating when patterns are hidden without a naming or grouping habit."
	]
	quest.12D1442268511209.quest_subtitle: "Scaling should stay readable."
	quest.12D1442268511209.title: "Manage multiple crafters cleanly"
	quest.12EC842F5A625A13.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the block used to encode crafting patterns."
		"Why this matters: The Pattern Grid turns recipes into instructions for the network. It is the bridge between manual crafting knowledge and machine-readable crafting logic."
		"Step by step: Place it near your Crafting Grid, power the network, and inspect the interface before encoding anything."
		"Common mistake: Encoding patterns without understanding the interface leads to recipes that do not behave as expected."
	]
	quest.12EC842F5A625A13.quest_subtitle: "Patterns are written here."
	quest.12EC842F5A625A13.title: "Craft a Pattern Grid"
	quest.13B60B25F0A8CC42.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Enriching Factory."
		"Why this matters: Factory machines process multiple items in parallel and are one of the clearest signs that your base is transitioning from workshop to industry."
		"Step by step: Replace or complement a single-machine step that you use constantly. Watch how throughput improves."
		"Common mistake: Factories still need power and input flow. More internal slots do not solve weak logistics by themselves."
	]
	quest.13B60B25F0A8CC42.quest_subtitle: "Parallel processing beats one-machine queues."
	quest.13B60B25F0A8CC42.title: "Build a Basic Factory"
	quest.15D4E134D8E5087A.quest_desc: [
		"Check four things in this order. One: is the source rotating? Two: is the shaft or cogwheel actually connected on the correct side? Three: is the network overstressed? Four: is the machine positioned exactly as its recipe expects?"
		"Create becomes much less mysterious when you solve it in that order."
		"Do not rebuild the whole contraption before you inspect the simple facts."
		"If one of the four checks fails, solve that single failure first and retest. Create problems become manageable when you isolate the first broken link."
	]
	quest.15D4E134D8E5087A.quest_subtitle: "Power, orientation, stress, recipe."
	quest.15D4E134D8E5087A.title: "When a Create machine does not move"
	quest.1679D91DF40BD693.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce an Elite Control Circuit."
		"Why this matters: Stellar Foundry’s later bridge recipes and advanced devices should feel supported by genuinely advanced industrial electronics. This is the material proof of that capability."
		"Step by step: Craft at least one now and note whether its prerequisite chain needs a future automation upgrade."
		"Common mistake: An elite circuit crafted once manually is progress; an elite circuit chain you can repeat is infrastructure."
	]
	quest.1679D91DF40BD693.quest_subtitle: "Your electronics tier is now mission-grade."
	quest.1679D91DF40BD693.title: "Craft an Elite Control Circuit"
	quest.17C85A1449323E7E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Pressurized Reaction Chamber."
		"Why this matters: This is one of the strongest midgame lessons in Mekanism: advanced recipes often combine multiple resource types and need a machine designed for that convergence."
		"Step by step: Set the block up in your chemistry area and inspect at least two useful recipes so you understand its role."
		"Common mistake: Supplying only some of the required inputs makes the machine appear broken."
	]
	quest.17C85A1449323E7E.quest_subtitle: "Items, fluids, gases, and power meet here."
	quest.17C85A1449323E7E.title: "Build a Pressurized Reaction Chamber"
	quest.18D54CC02E20698E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Ultimate Control Circuit."
		"Why this matters: This item is a compact symbol of a mature Mekanism industrial base. It requires that several earlier material chains have become manageable."
		"Step by step: Craft at least one and treat it as a quality bar: if it was misery, improve the prerequisite automation."
		"Common mistake: Endgame components are supposed to test your systems, not your patience for chest searching."
	]
	quest.18D54CC02E20698E.quest_subtitle: "Complete the control-circuit ladder."
	quest.18D54CC02E20698E.title: "Reach Ultimate control"
	quest.197CE97BD49028AD.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Set up repeatable crafting support for a high-value space-program component."
		"Why this matters: Good candidates include Orbital Guidance Chips, Pressure Sealant, Rocket Flight Computers, or a similar advanced chain you repeatedly need."
		"Step by step: Use Refined Storage autocrafting, modular logistics, or a deliberate factory workflow to reduce manual recipe repetition."
		"Common mistake: If a component still requires you to search every chest, the endgame has not absorbed that lesson yet."
	]
	quest.197CE97BD49028AD.quest_subtitle: "Bridge items should no longer be handcrafted every time."
	quest.197CE97BD49028AD.title: "Automate an advanced mission component"
	quest.1D499E4B14A07F0A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Prepare dedicated fuel hardware for the rocket system."
		"Why this matters: Stellaris vehicle preparation uses dedicated modules and tank capacity. Building these now prevents last-minute recipe scrambling beside the pad."
		"Step by step: Craft a Fuel Module and a Tier 1 Tank so you have the core parts expected for first-flight preparation."
		"Common mistake: A rocket with no practical fuel-handling plan is only half assembled."
	]
	quest.1D499E4B14A07F0A.quest_subtitle: "The vehicle needs more than a loose bucket."
	quest.1D499E4B14A07F0A.title: "Craft a Fuel Module or tank path"
	quest.1D63069B6A6C7B5B.quest_desc: [
		"Open the Autocrafting Monitor first. It often reveals the missing ingredient or step immediately."
		"Then verify the pattern mode, whether the Autocrafter is connected, whether external machines accept the required input, and whether outputs can return to the network."
		"Autocrafting failures are usually honest messages about missing setup, not random bugs."
		"Change one variable at a time. If you alter patterns, machine sides, import paths, and ingredients all at once, the real fix becomes harder to identify."
	]
	quest.1D63069B6A6C7B5B.quest_subtitle: "Pattern, ingredients, machine path, missing outputs."
	quest.1D63069B6A6C7B5B.title: "When autocrafting fails"
	quest.1E61799885D0D37A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Sophisticated Backpack for exploration and building."
		"Why this matters: A full inventory is one of the biggest distractions in a technical progression pack. The backpack lets you carry tools, ore, and building materials without constant return trips."
		"Step by step: Craft the basic backpack now. Later chapters introduce stronger storage systems, but this remains useful for expeditions."
		"Common mistake: Do not treat the backpack as your main base storage. It is mobile support, not a warehouse."
	]
	quest.1E61799885D0D37A.quest_subtitle: "Inventory pressure disappears early in this pack."
	quest.1E61799885D0D37A.title: "Make a backpack"
	quest.1FBFAF4DBB8B9AED.quest_desc: [
		"Create machines use rotation. Most modern tech machines use Forge Energy, often abbreviated FE. This chapter starts your FE grid."
		"Keep the distinction clear: a Powah cable cannot power a Mechanical Press, and a Create shaft cannot power a Mekanism machine."
		"Once you understand this split, the rest of the pack becomes much easier to read."
		"Whenever a machine stalls later, first ask the correct question: does it need rotational force, FE, pressure, or something else entirely?"
	]
	quest.1FBFAF4DBB8B9AED.quest_subtitle: "Create rotation and Forge Energy are not interchangeable."
	quest.1FBFAF4DBB8B9AED.title: "Two power systems, two purposes"
	quest.20CEE5E0DBD736F4.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter exists because beginner-friendly modpacks need more than recipes. They need a way to diagnose common problems without forcing players to search the internet for every symptom."
		"You can read these quests at any time. They are intentionally written as compact problem-solving notes."
		"Complete only the entries you have read and understood."
		"Use this chapter like an internal manual. Reading one relevant note before rebuilding a system can save far more time than the checkmark costs."
	]
	quest.20CEE5E0DBD736F4.quest_subtitle: "These quests are not progression gates."
	quest.20CEE5E0DBD736F4.title: "Reference chapter: use this whenever you get stuck"
	quest.21B92A2470962CAE.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Infusion Crystal."
		"Why this matters: Essence upgrading should become a deliberate, repeatable process rather than an occasional inventory scramble."
		"Use it as the first serious quality-of-life tool of the chapter."
		"Keep the crystal in a dedicated cultivation crafting area so it does not vanish into a random backpack between upgrades."
		"Repeated recipes become calmer when the key reusable ingredient always has an obvious home."
	]
	quest.21B92A2470962CAE.quest_subtitle: "A small crystal makes a long progression smoother."
	quest.21B92A2470962CAE.title: "Stabilize crafting with an Infusion Crystal"
	quest.21C7E50F6C6EFCC9.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Plant Sower."
		"Why this matters: Long space projects are easier when basic food and plant resources do not require your constant attention."
		"Step by step: Place it near a farm area only after checking its working range and power needs."
		"Common mistake: A machine with no shaped farm layout will appear inefficient even when it is functioning normally."
	]
	quest.21C7E50F6C6EFCC9.quest_subtitle: "Plant Sower begins a sustainable food loop."
	quest.21C7E50F6C6EFCC9.title: "Automate crop planting"
	quest.228EF8B659E2ED12.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft and insert a 1k Storage Disk."
		"Why this matters: The first disk proves the network works. Later you will upgrade capacity or offload bulk resources to drawers and external storage."
		"Step by step: Place the disk in the drive and move a few different item types into the Grid to verify capacity increases and item search works."
		"Common mistake: Do not judge digital storage by the size of the first disk. This is a foundation, not an endpoint."
	]
	quest.228EF8B659E2ED12.quest_subtitle: "Small is fine when the system is new."
	quest.228EF8B659E2ED12.title: "Insert a 1k Storage Disk"
	quest.229690369447FB84.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Exchanging Gadget."
		"Why this matters: As your factory matures, temporary cobblestone floors may become metal walkways, and launch-area placeholders may become themed blocks. Renovation tools keep that process pleasant."
		"Step by step: Test the gadget on a small wall or floor segment before applying it to critical structures."
		"Common mistake: Do not renovate a functional machine room without understanding what blocks are safe to replace."
	]
	quest.229690369447FB84.quest_subtitle: "Renovation should not punish iteration."
	quest.229690369447FB84.title: "Use an Exchanging Gadget"
	quest.22AA3AD9CB9C5831.quest_desc: [
		"Use the Encased Fan with water to process a valid washing recipe. This proves that your fan setup is correctly oriented and powered."
		"Bulk washing matters because it can handle piles of items at once. It is one of the first moments where Create clearly outperforms manual crafting."
		"Keep the layout readable: fan, water, item area, and a safe collection point."
		"Use this setup as a reusable learning rig: once you understand washing, later fan-based recipes will feel much easier to diagnose and scale."
	]
	quest.22AA3AD9CB9C5831.quest_subtitle: "A visible, teachable automation step."
	quest.22AA3AD9CB9C5831.title: "Wash items in bulk"
	quest.22DA172CB9D3DB6F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Pressure Tubes and begin a small pressure line."
		"Why this matters: Tubes store and move compressed air. A larger network behaves differently from a tiny line, so learn with a compact setup first."
		"Step by step: Connect the compressor to a short tube line. Keep the path visible and avoid burying it before you understand it."
		"Common mistake: Treating pressure tubes like cosmetic pipes leads to confusing failures."
	]
	quest.22DA172CB9D3DB6F.quest_subtitle: "These are not energy cables."
	quest.22DA172CB9D3DB6F.title: "Route pressure with tubes"
	quest.2308A03F10CFDEF4.quest_desc: [
		"Mekanism is the main high-tech processing route in Stellar Foundry. It starts with simple enriched materials and later expands into chemicals, gases, ore scaling, and precision control."
		"For beginners, the key habit is simple: inspect machine sides, watch energy, and read the recipe category in JEI before assuming a machine is wrong."
		"This chapter introduces the core machine chain one piece at a time."
		"Keep the first Mekanism machines close enough that you can watch them together. Early comprehension matters more than immediately spreading into a huge hall."
	]
	quest.2308A03F10CFDEF4.quest_subtitle: "This mod becomes the industrial spine of the pack."
	quest.2308A03F10CFDEF4.title: "Enter Mekanism"
	quest.23677EEFC7C63099.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Engineer’s Hammer."
		"Why this matters: Immersive Engineering structures often form from block arrangements rather than single recipes. The hammer is central to that workflow."
		"Step by step: Keep it in a tool slot or a dedicated engineering chest. You will need it repeatedly when assembling machines."
		"Common mistake: Trying to form multiblocks without the correct tool creates unnecessary confusion."
	]
	quest.23677EEFC7C63099.quest_subtitle: "Multiblocks need a construction tool."
	quest.23677EEFC7C63099.title: "Craft the Engineer’s Hammer"
	quest.23A472873C170D11.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Return with Moon Stone from the Moon as direct proof that the first expedition reached its intended destination."
		"Why this matters: The pack uses material proof so that exploration chapters are not only self-reported achievements."
		"Step by step: Gather at least a small sample during your first excursion and store it in a clearly marked research area back at base."
		"Common mistake: Returning empty-handed makes it harder to connect exploration with industry."
	]
	quest.23A472873C170D11.quest_subtitle: "A physical proof that exploration happened."
	quest.23A472873C170D11.title: "Bring back Moon Stone"
	quest.23CA6A230A408FCA.quest_desc: [
		"Complete this after finishing several mastery challenges and feeling that your world is not merely complete, but deliberate: readable factories, repeatable launch systems, useful colonies, and a visual identity."
		"This is not needed to claim the main pack victory. It is the badge for players who turned Stellar Foundry into their own long-term engineering world."
		"Congratulations on mastering the pack’s philosophy."
		"Use this as a celebration point. By now, the questbook should feel like the record of a world you engineered, not merely a list you cleared."
	]
	quest.23CA6A230A408FCA.quest_subtitle: "A final optional badge for a deeply developed world."
	quest.23CA6A230A408FCA.title: "Mastery charter"
	quest.241BD6937C5F55A5.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Grid and connect it to the Controller."
		"Why this matters: The Grid is your access screen. It lets you search, inspect, and move items without opening twenty inventories."
		"Step by step: Place it somewhere you naturally stand when crafting and planning. Good access placement matters."
		"Common mistake: A digital network hidden behind machines is technically correct and practically annoying."
	]
	quest.241BD6937C5F55A5.quest_subtitle: "Searchable access is the whole point."
	quest.241BD6937C5F55A5.title: "Add a Grid"
	quest.24367A7C6F424AF1.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft and attach a Pressure Gauge."
		"Why this matters: The gauge tells you whether the system is building, holding, or losing pressure. It is a vital teaching tool and a vital safety tool."
		"Step by step: Attach it where you can see it while testing machines. Watch how the reading changes under load."
		"Common mistake: Expanding a system with no gauge is like building an energy grid with no idea whether it is charged."
	]
	quest.24367A7C6F424AF1.quest_subtitle: "Read your system before expanding it."
	quest.24367A7C6F424AF1.title: "Add a Pressure Gauge"
	quest.24D27BDD168EE345.quest_desc: [
		"A launch-and-return loop is exciting, but colonies are where the pack’s long-term identity lives. The project chapter gave every major destination a role; now one or more of those roles should become a real, survivable, expandable base."
		"This chapter uses checkmarks for design decisions and item tasks for clear infrastructure pieces. You are expected to build thoughtfully, not copy a single prescribed blueprint."
		"Start modestly. Reliability comes before scale."
		"A colony should answer three questions: why does it exist, how does it stay supplied, and what useful work can it perform without constant babysitting?"
	]
	quest.24D27BDD168EE345.quest_subtitle: "A true space pack needs a reason to stay."
	quest.24D27BDD168EE345.title: "From missions to colonies"
	quest.25DB9D5578EB709C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Obtain an Empowered Restonia Crystal."
		"Why this matters: This proves the Empowerer setup is complete and that the branch has reached its advanced materials layer."
		"Keep one sample as a reference while you decide whether to scale the system."
		"Watch the entire process once from input to result. Seeing the flow makes later automation and troubleshooting much less abstract."
		"Treat the empowered crystal as proof that the branch now has a complete advanced-material loop, not as a single trophy."
	]
	quest.25DB9D5578EB709C.quest_subtitle: "Advanced optional materials should feel deliberate."
	quest.25DB9D5578EB709C.title: "Produce an empowered crystal"
	quest.2670B727DB86E7DA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Process your first Energized Steel in the Orb."
		"Why this matters: This proves that the energy grid and the Powah processing station actually work together. Many later upgrades depend on this material philosophy."
		"Step by step: Check the recipe in JEI, place ingredients into the Orb, and confirm the Rod supplies energy until completion."
		"Common mistake: If the Orb never progresses, diagnose power input before crafting replacements."
	]
	quest.2670B727DB86E7DA.quest_subtitle: "The first Powah material milestone."
	quest.2670B727DB86E7DA.title: "Create Energized Steel"
	quest.26E44AD5305C2D6E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft several blank Patterns."
		"Why this matters: A single pattern proves the system. A small stack lets you immediately solve several repeated component recipes, such as common storage or machine parts."
		"Step by step: Craft at least eight patterns and keep a few unused until you identify bottlenecks."
		"Common mistake: Do not encode patterns randomly. Choose recipes you actually repeat."
	]
	quest.26E44AD5305C2D6E.quest_subtitle: "Autocrafting needs recipe carriers."
	quest.26E44AD5305C2D6E.title: "Prepare empty Patterns"
	quest.273CAD26DD3D4992.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Replace scattered temporary chest piles with at least one intentional storage area."
		"Why this matters: A factory only feels controllable when materials are easy to find. Organized storage reduces downtime more than many players expect."
		"Step by step: Choose one wall or room, keep frequently used resources near crafting, and reserve a section for mod-specific components."
		"Common mistake: If you cannot find your own plates, circuits, or alloys, automation will feel slower than it is."
		"Iron Chests fits this chapter as a straightforward physical-storage upgrade when a normal chest wall becomes cramped."
	]
	quest.273CAD26DD3D4992.quest_subtitle: "Storage is part of engineering."
	quest.273CAD26DD3D4992.title: "Stop using random chests"
	quest.2792A8C76128D7B4.quest_desc: [
		"Run several of your existing machines at once and watch energy behavior. Does storage drain slowly, collapse instantly, or remain stable?"
		"Use that observation to decide whether the next improvement should be generation, storage, cable layout, or machine scheduling."
		"Completing this quest honestly will save you far more time than chasing bigger blocks without diagnosis."
		"When demand spikes, solve the bottleneck deliberately: generation, transfer capacity, buffering, or machine timing. Guessing creates expensive clutter."
	]
	quest.2792A8C76128D7B4.quest_subtitle: "Power failures are usually system failures."
	quest.2792A8C76128D7B4.title: "Review cable capacity and machine demand"
	quest.27E6D4B7F4E42BD5.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Mercury Solar Lens."
		"Why this matters: Solerium, higher-tier Powah parts, and precision guidance become a single project that clearly points toward high-energy off-world infrastructure."
		"This is the cleanest RC4 example of a planet receiving a dedicated long-term identity."
		"Use the Lens as a cue to plan high-energy infrastructure rather than a single collectible. Mercury should now imply a future industrial role."
	]
	quest.27E6D4B7F4E42BD5.quest_subtitle: "Mercury becomes an energy-development destination."
	quest.27E6D4B7F4E42BD5.title: "Focus a Mercury Solar Lens"
	quest.2963CD29511B0068.quest_desc: [
		"Before digital storage appears, get comfortable with the storage logic you will keep using forever: input chest, processing machine, output storage, and overflow protection."
		"Sketch or physically build one tiny example using your existing Create line. It does not need to be beautiful. It needs to be understandable."
		"This mental model transfers directly to Refined Storage, XNet, Modular Routers, and planetary bases."
		"A storage layout that explains itself is worth more than one that saves a few blocks. Readability becomes a form of performance in long worlds."
	]
	quest.2963CD29511B0068.quest_subtitle: "Think input, buffer, output."
	quest.2963CD29511B0068.title: "Connect storage to machines conceptually"
	quest.29BB16753A520CD6.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Electrolytic Separator."
		"Why this matters: This machine opens chemical production with gases. It is a major step because the pack’s later infrastructure uses more than items and FE."
		"Step by step: Place it in a dedicated chemistry section or at least reserve space for tanks, pipes, and future gas handling."
		"Common mistake: If your chemistry blocks are scattered among unrelated machines, every later gas route is harder to read."
	]
	quest.29BB16753A520CD6.quest_subtitle: "Gases become part of your industrial language."
	quest.29BB16753A520CD6.title: "Introduce Electrolytic Separation"
	quest.2C7AC14D1B4C16E9.quest_desc: [
		"Use the Flux Plug, Flux Point, and your chosen power source to support at least one remote consumer reliably. A launch-area support block, distant factory machine, or colony utility machine all qualify."
		"Watch the system under load for a moment. The quest is about confidence, not simply placing blocks."
		"If the remote endpoint starves, improve generation, buffers, or network setup before calling the route finished."
		"Remote power is only solved when the consumer survives normal demand, not merely when one block flashes active for a moment."
	]
	quest.2C7AC14D1B4C16E9.quest_subtitle: "A network is real when a distant machine stays powered."
	quest.2C7AC14D1B4C16E9.title: "Prove a remote energy route"
	quest.2C84005EB2AB797D.quest_desc: [
		"Optional chapters serve different player motivations: more building, more factory style, more advanced networks, or more resource automation."
		"Follow the main numbered route whenever you want clarity. Enter optional systems when they solve a problem or inspire a project."
		"A perfect playthrough is not one that uses every mod. It is one that uses systems intentionally."
		"Optional chapters are excellent when they answer a real desire: better aesthetics, deeper storage, renewable resources, or another style of engineering."
	]
	quest.2C84005EB2AB797D.quest_subtitle: "Optional does not mean useless."
	quest.2C84005EB2AB797D.title: "When to use optional chapters"
	quest.2CBA6A7FEE1C5C5C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Actually Additions Crusher."
		"Why this matters: It gives the optional branch its own local material-processing identity without displacing the main Mekanism/Create route."
		"Use it where its recipes solve a real bottleneck."
		"Compare its role with processors you already know. Optional machines are valuable when they offer a satisfying local solution or recipe path."
		"Use it where its recipes justify the space, not merely because every mod block must exist somewhere in the base."
	]
	quest.2CBA6A7FEE1C5C5C.quest_subtitle: "A side processor should earn its floor space."
	quest.2CBA6A7FEE1C5C5C.title: "Add a Crusher for AA processing"
	quest.2CCEDEB36835830C.quest_desc: [
		"You now have several ways to move items: Create logistics, Refined Storage interfaces, Modular Routers, and XNet. The best choice is the simplest tool that solves the current job cleanly."
		"Review your factory and remove one manual handoff that annoyed you during the last hour."
		"Good automation is visible relief. You should feel it immediately."
		"If a routing solution is hard to explain in one sentence, simplify it before it grows. Future expansion should inherit clarity, not confusion."
	]
	quest.2CCEDEB36835830C.quest_subtitle: "Your base should now feel calmer."
	quest.2CCEDEB36835830C.title: "Factory routing checkpoint"
	quest.2D68F28393384B3F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Rocket Controls."
		"Why this matters: This block is a required part of the addon’s rocket logic and makes the route feel like a vehicle build rather than a static machine recipe."
		"Step by step: Craft it and keep it with the other rocket structural parts before assembly."
		"Common mistake: Misplacing one required structural block can prevent a constructed rocket from behaving as expected."
	]
	quest.2D68F28393384B3F.quest_subtitle: "A vehicle needs pilot control."
	quest.2D68F28393384B3F.title: "Prepare rocket control blocks"
	quest.2E3AC46593015230.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Copper Wire."
		"Why this matters: Wires turn the chapter from theory into infrastructure and create a visible bridge from materials to electrical layouts."
		"Keep a small stock if you intend to continue."
		"Treat wire as a stocked intermediate, not as a panic craft when the next connector recipe appears."
		"Repeated electrical crafts become smoother when conductors already live in a visible, organized buffer."
	]
	quest.2E3AC46593015230.quest_subtitle: "A power system starts with conductors."
	quest.2E3AC46593015230.title: "Produce Copper Wire"
	quest.2EF00F858C9B8CAA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Iron Autocrafter from ExtraStorage."
		"Why this matters: Once you start encoding repeated components, larger crafters reduce block sprawl and make automation rooms easier to read."
		"Step by step: Move a sensible group of related patterns into the upgraded crafter, such as common machine components or storage parts."
		"Common mistake: More pattern slots help only when patterns are grouped intentionally."
	]
	quest.2EF00F858C9B8CAA.quest_subtitle: "Larger factories deserve denser pattern hubs."
	quest.2EF00F858C9B8CAA.title: "Upgrade into ExtraStorage autocrafting"
	quest.2FA50C38741489E8.quest_desc: [
		"Stellar Foundry now gives remote logistics a dedicated progression step before permanent colonies. Ender Storage handles compact cross-dimensional item and fluid transfer, while Flux Networks supports wireless FE routing between distant sites."
		"This chapter is deliberately placed after deeper space planning and stronger power. The goal is not to skip logistics, but to design the backbone that makes outposts, launchpads, and remote workshops feel intentional."
		"Read the quests as a small infrastructure project: first move resources, then move energy, then prove the systems remain understandable."
		"The objective is not to erase distance completely. It is to make distance manageable through channels, buffers, and power routes that stay understandable."
	]
	quest.2FA50C38741489E8.quest_subtitle: "Colonies should feel connected, not isolated."
	quest.2FA50C38741489E8.title: "Turn multiple bases into one system"
	quest.3010B88609A6B955.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Etching Tank and UV Light Box."
		"Why this matters: PneumaticCraft circuits are a deliberate process. This chapter teaches you to follow a multi-stage technical recipe without skipping the support blocks."
		"Step by step: Set the blocks up in one local work area and inspect the recipe chain for Printed Circuit Boards."
		"Common mistake: Spreading a multi-stage process across the base makes it feel harder than it is."
	]
	quest.3010B88609A6B955.quest_subtitle: "Etching and UV work reward patience."
	quest.3010B88609A6B955.title: "Prepare circuit manufacturing tools"
	quest.305F0CED038B7C89.quest_desc: [
		"Pick one family of recurring technical components and make it truly comfortable to request, replenish, or batch-produce."
		"A family means several related outputs, not one single item. Examples: multiple Mekanism circuit tiers, Create precision components, or a mission-prep component suite."
		"The reward is a factory that feels smarter."
		"Document the chosen family clearly or place its main controls together. A mastered automation chain should be easy to use when you return days later."
	]
	quest.305F0CED038B7C89.quest_subtitle: "Choose circuits, alloys, precision parts, or mission components."
	quest.305F0CED038B7C89.title: "Automate a full technical component family"
	quest.30E596CAF485A66D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Drawer Key and understand why locking matters."
		"Why this matters: Locked drawers keep their item identity even when empty. This prevents an automation line from assigning the wrong resource to an open slot."
		"Step by step: Lock drawers that belong to automated production, especially common outputs such as nuggets, ingots, and plates."
		"Common mistake: Unlocked empty drawers in a factory are invitations for accidental misrouting."
	]
	quest.30E596CAF485A66D.quest_subtitle: "A simple protection against storage chaos."
	quest.30E596CAF485A66D.title: "Learn drawer locking"
	quest.32640FE5EDD34938.quest_desc: [
		"This tier uses four patches that define a self-supporting technical base: Mekanism, autocrafting, routing, and pressure-era components."
		"Why this matters: players often quit when a pack feels like isolated crafts. This tier rewards the point where systems finally lock together."
		"Reward: an industrial seal, XP, and a pickup upgrade that makes long factory and mining sessions smoother. The seal activates Factory Rhythm when right-clicked."
		"Use the reward as a gentle signal that the factory now deserves permanent zones, cleaner routes, and stronger maintenance habits."
	]
	quest.32640FE5EDD34938.quest_subtitle: "Your factory now has real systems, not just machines."
	quest.32640FE5EDD34938.title: "Milestone Tier II: Industrial Systems"
	quest.3353639DE69DBA97.quest_desc: [
		"The next Stellaris phase asks you to treat off-world travel as a continuing program. New destinations, harsher environments, and rarer materials reward better logistics and stronger preparation."
		"Your expanded Mekanism and Powah infrastructure should now support longer mission chains without constant manual recovery. This chapter follows a clear resource route: Mars for Plutonium, Venus for Neptunium and Corronium, Mercury for Solerium."
		"Do not skip planning just because the first launch succeeded."
		"Upgrade the preparation process, not only the gear. Longer missions should feel better organized than the first one, not more chaotic."
	]
	quest.3353639DE69DBA97.quest_subtitle: "The first moon trip was training, not the finale."
	quest.3353639DE69DBA97.title: "Deeper destinations require stronger preparation"
	quest.3362BA64E9BF2654.quest_desc: [
		"Choose a simple processed material and make it flow through a small loop: ingredients are supplied, a machine processes them, and outputs return to organized storage."
		"This does not need to be a giant autocrafting plant. It should be easy to explain and easy to debug."
		"If the loop stalls, diagnose the bottleneck instead of adding random extra pipes."
		"Write a tiny rule for the loop in your head: what enters, what leaves, and where excess goes. Clear intent prevents invisible item traffic later."
	]
	quest.3362BA64E9BF2654.quest_subtitle: "Machine input, machine output, storage return."
	quest.3362BA64E9BF2654.title: "Build one complete logistics loop"
	quest.33938635557937E4.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce Plastic through the PneumaticCraft route."
		"Why this matters: Stellar Foundry uses pressure-era materials as a bridge toward high-end components. Plastic helps make the space program feel industrial instead of purely vanilla-crafted."
		"Step by step: Use the Pressure Chamber or required recipe route and make a small reserve."
		"Common mistake: If you treat every plastic piece as a one-off craft, space-prep recipes will become tedious."
	]
	quest.33938635557937E4.quest_subtitle: "Plastic connects pressure tech to space preparation."
	quest.33938635557937E4.title: "Craft Pneumatic Plastic"
	quest.35D29DC282503956.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Safe for valuables or memorable mission items."
		"Why this matters: Not every storage block needs to be optimized for throughput. A safe is perfect for a colony charter copy, rare finds, or personal world keepsakes."
		"Step by step: Place it somewhere intentional and decide what category of items belongs there."
		"Common mistake: Sentimental or rare items disappear in large digital systems when you never give them a special home."
	]
	quest.35D29DC282503956.quest_subtitle: "Supplementaries adds practical decorative utility."
	quest.35D29DC282503956.title: "Protect important valuables"
	quest.3611D22F7926BF4E.quest_desc: [
		"Group systems by purpose: Create workshop, FE grid, Mekanism processing, chemistry, storage, launch logistics, and colony staging."
		"Leave walking space and service corridors. Put buffers where they explain flow. Label with visual design when possible."
		"A slightly larger but readable factory ages far better than a compact maze."
		"Leave empty space intentionally. Expansion corridors, maintenance gaps, and visible cable routes are part of the build, not wasted floor area."
	]
	quest.3611D22F7926BF4E.quest_subtitle: "Zones, backbones, and visible service paths."
	quest.3611D22F7926BF4E.title: "How to avoid factory spaghetti"
	quest.36E2EE9F4B4AB0CD.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Basic Processors for network hardware."
		"Why this matters: This is the first point where digital storage feels like engineering instead of chest replacement. Processors turn simple materials into network infrastructure."
		"Step by step: Make several processors and keep them with other machine components."
		"Common mistake: Losing processors in an unsorted chest is exactly the problem this chapter is trying to solve."
	]
	quest.36E2EE9F4B4AB0CD.quest_subtitle: "Digital storage uses electronic components."
	quest.36E2EE9F4B4AB0CD.title: "Prepare Basic Processors"
	quest.379F0A62DC909EF7.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Quantum Bridge Card."
		"Why this matters: This card is the AE2 branch’s answer to large-world convenience, enabling wireless-terminal use through a quantum bridge and across dimensions when the rest of the setup supports it."
		"Step by step: Treat it as an advanced network accessory, not a starter item."
		"Common mistake: A card is only one part of a real cross-dimensional AE2 access plan."
	]
	quest.379F0A62DC909EF7.quest_subtitle: "Optional AE2 access now reaches across dimensions."
	quest.379F0A62DC909EF7.title: "Prepare a Quantum Bridge Card"
	quest.386472F5A38C1224.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basin and Mechanical Mixer."
		"Why this matters: Mixing introduces recipes that combine multiple ingredients with rotation, and later with heat. This is an important bridge toward brass and more advanced Create components."
		"Step by step: Place the Mixer directly above the Basin, connect rotational power, and verify the mixer head can reach the basin."
		"Common mistake: A Mixer placed beside the Basin will not process recipes."
	]
	quest.386472F5A38C1224.quest_subtitle: "Recipes now happen inside a processing station."
	quest.386472F5A38C1224.title: "Build a Basin and Mixer"
	quest.392332DC65C4308F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce a starter reserve of Basic Control Circuits."
		"Why this matters: Mekanism machines quickly consume circuits in batches. Crafting one circuit only when a recipe asks for it slows every unlock."
		"Step by step: Use the Infuser as intended and produce at least eight circuits. Store the leftovers in your component area."
		"Common mistake: If recipe ingredients look correct but nothing happens, confirm the Infuser has the right secondary material."
	]
	quest.392332DC65C4308F.quest_subtitle: "These are the language of Mekanism recipes."
	quest.392332DC65C4308F.title: "Make Basic Control Circuits"
	quest.39CCBE8A6A0714C3.quest_desc: [
		"Create a small archive room, control center, or mission wall that displays your progress: major badges, rare materials, maps, or thematic records."
		"This is a worldbuilding challenge and a celebration of the progression path."
		"A modpack becomes memorable when the world tells the story of how it grew."
		"A written archive makes the world feel finished in a way a chest of trophies never can. Record the logic behind your favorite systems."
	]
	quest.39CCBE8A6A0714C3.quest_subtitle: "Give the story a place to live."
	quest.39CCBE8A6A0714C3.title: "Archive your world’s progress"
	quest.3B199F9C999ABC9F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Continue the Venus resource route and obtain Corronium Ingots."
		"Why this matters: Stellar Foundry wants exploration to feed industry. Corronium represents the kind of resource that justifies returning to space repeatedly."
		"Step by step: Bring back a sample and review which later recipes or upgrades it enables in your installed version."
		"Common mistake: If a destination has valuable output, consider planning a stable outpost instead of repeating unprepared raids."
	]
	quest.3B199F9C999ABC9F.quest_subtitle: "The program reaches high-value exotic materials."
	quest.3B199F9C999ABC9F.title: "Acquire Corronium"
	quest.3B468738D5A17CA5.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce a small stockpile of Andesite Alloy."
		"Why this matters: This material appears in shafts, cogwheels, basic machines, casings, and many supporting parts. Create becomes frustrating when you craft it one piece at a time."
		"Step by step: Make at least sixteen alloy now. Treat it as your first factory material, not as a rare trophy."
		"Common mistake: Underproducing Andesite Alloy leads to constant recipe interruptions."
	]
	quest.3B468738D5A17CA5.quest_subtitle: "Your first industrial material."
	quest.3B468738D5A17CA5.title: "Craft Andesite Alloy"
	quest.3BB64FF84FB5811D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Advanced Control Circuit before assembling guidance hardware."
		"Why this matters: This makes the transition into space feel earned by your existing Mekanism line. Your launch systems should be supported by more than beginner electronics."
		"Step by step: Use your Infuser and alloy chain to create the circuit, then keep it near the other mission components."
		"Common mistake: If this single circuit is painful, produce a few extra alloys now and improve the bottleneck after the first launch."
	]
	quest.3BB64FF84FB5811D.quest_subtitle: "The space program needs a step beyond starter circuits."
	quest.3BB64FF84FB5811D.title: "Upgrade electronics for mission control"
	quest.3BF0EC1FD84DFADE.quest_desc: [
		"By now you have machines, storage, and power. The next skill is deciding where items should go, when they should move, and what happens if a destination fills."
		"This chapter introduces flexible logistics tools. Use them to make production lines cleaner, not to hide a setup you no longer understand."
		"A strong factory has readable routes and controlled outputs."
		"Pipez offers direct utility routing, while Create Ender Storage and XNet Gases add optional specialist links for players who want more compact cross-system logistics."
	]
	quest.3BF0EC1FD84DFADE.quest_subtitle: "Moving items is not the same as solving logistics."
	quest.3BF0EC1FD84DFADE.title: "Automation means routing decisions"
	quest.3CF1BDB4A278DEF5.quest_desc: [
		"This optional chapter now ends after you have turned the addon's machines and structural pieces into a real first prototype, not just a parts checklist."
		"You have the core tables, machines, controls, structure blocks, environmental support pieces, and one validated starting build required to continue experimenting responsibly."
		"Use this route when you want a more build-driven space engineering project beside the main Stellaris progression."
		"This branch is complete when you understand the addon's build language well enough to continue designing confidently without the questbook holding every step."
	]
	quest.3CF1BDB4A278DEF5.quest_subtitle: "You now understand the alternate rocket philosophy."
	quest.3CF1BDB4A278DEF5.title: "Create-route project complete"
	quest.3DAE48F09170F8EE.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Start a reliable food loop before the machine chapters become absorbing."
		"Why this matters: The pack contains Farmer’s Delight, but you do not need complex meals immediately. You only need a repeatable food source that prevents mining trips from ending early."
		"Step by step: Secure crops or animal food, cook a useful stack, and keep several meals in your backpack."
		"Common mistake: Ignoring food creates unnecessary deaths and breaks the flow of technical learning."
	]
	quest.3DAE48F09170F8EE.quest_subtitle: "A hungry engineer makes poor decisions."
	quest.3DAE48F09170F8EE.title: "Prepare food before industry"
	quest.3E8CE0961FB87266.quest_desc: [
		"This tier completes when you have claimed the Workshop, Create Engineer, Grid Operator, and Storage Architect patches from the early main route."
		"Why this matters: it proves that your world has moved beyond survival and into a real workshop/factory foundation."
		"Reward: a dedicated milestone seal, XP, and a practical starter stack upgrade for backpack storage. The seal can be right-clicked to activate the Workshop Focus Field Protocol."
		"This is the earliest reward tier and should arrive naturally if the foundation chapters were played with care instead of skipped mechanically."
	]
	quest.3E8CE0961FB87266.quest_subtitle: "4 early milestone patches -> Foundation reward tier."
	quest.3E8CE0961FB87266.title: "Milestone Tier I: Foundations"
	quest.3F095CBC7F4AA77C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Atomic Reconstructor."
		"Why this matters: It is the signature conversion machine of Actually Additions and opens the resource-transforming part of the addon."
		"Start with a clean test area so laser-based conversions are easy to observe."
		"Try at least one visible reconstruction conversion after crafting the block so you understand the machine as a process, not just as a recipe requirement."
		"Keep the beam path obvious while learning. Readability matters whenever a machine interacts with the world instead of a private GUI."
	]
	quest.3F095CBC7F4AA77C.quest_subtitle: "The addon begins with precise reconstruction."
	quest.3F095CBC7F4AA77C.title: "Build the Atomic Reconstructor"
	quest.3F5867C163959E6E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Drawer Controller."
		"Why this matters: The controller turns a drawer wall into a connected storage area. Later automation can insert into the network through one point instead of targeting every drawer."
		"Step by step: Place the controller near your drawer area and confirm it reaches the drawers you expect."
		"Common mistake: Controllers have range rules. A drawer visually nearby may still be outside your actual setup."
	]
	quest.3F5867C163959E6E.quest_subtitle: "One access point beats twenty manual clicks."
	quest.3F5867C163959E6E.title: "Control a drawer network"
	quest.41A84D8907F130A0.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Obtain Desh Ingots from Stellaris progression."
		"Why this matters: A good space modpack makes destinations matter. New materials should unlock new equipment, upgrades, or mission capability."
		"Step by step: Collect a starter sample and check its uses in JEI. Let the item tell you what the next destination makes possible."
		"Common mistake: Treating new planetary metals as trophies rather than recipe materials misses the point of progression."
	]
	quest.41A84D8907F130A0.quest_subtitle: "New worlds should expand your material vocabulary."
	quest.41A84D8907F130A0.title: "Analyze Desh"
	quest.41B31EF1EECECAAC.quest_desc: [
		"Before launch, verify all of the following: the rocket is in place, launch hardware is correct, fuel production works, your full suit is ready, oxygen support is prepared, and your mission loadout is packed."
		"This quest is intentionally a checkmark because readiness is a player decision. Use it honestly."
		"Once complete, your first off-world mission is unlocked."
		"When the checklist starts to feel almost boring, it is doing its job. Reliability should become routine before the first serious expedition."
	]
	quest.41B31EF1EECECAAC.quest_subtitle: "Rocket, pad, fuel, suit, oxygen, supplies."
	quest.41B31EF1EECECAAC.title: "Final first-launch checklist"
	quest.42A751AF7C51F18B.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Oil Finder and understand where your fuel source comes from."
		"Why this matters: Repeated launches require a repeatable fuel source. Searching randomly every time is not a long-term plan."
		"Step by step: Use the Oil Finder according to its tooltip or guide, identify an oil source, and mark the location or access path clearly."
		"Common mistake: If you never record resource locations, future missions inherit today’s confusion."
	]
	quest.42A751AF7C51F18B.quest_subtitle: "Fuel begins with a resource plan."
	quest.42A751AF7C51F18B.title: "Find and process oil"
	quest.4326D65687A64E0C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce the foundation material for your digital network."
		"Why this matters: Refined Storage recipes build on this component repeatedly. Making a real batch now prevents the first network from stalling halfway through."
		"Step by step: Use JEI, gather ingredients, and craft at least sixteen Quartz Enriched Iron."
		"Common mistake: Do not craft only the exact number for one block. The grid, controller, and drive all compete for the same materials."
	]
	quest.4326D65687A64E0C.quest_subtitle: "The first Refined Storage material."
	quest.4326D65687A64E0C.title: "Craft Quartz Enriched Iron"
	quest.43FA492D62D8EFE2.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Big Oxygen Tank."
		"Why this matters: Off-world exploration becomes more comfortable and safer when survival resources last longer. Capacity upgrades are not vanity; they change mission range."
		"Step by step: Craft the tank and update your mission checklist so it replaces or supplements the earlier oxygen plan."
		"Common mistake: Using starter survival gear forever often turns progression into unnecessary pressure."
	]
	quest.43FA492D62D8EFE2.quest_subtitle: "Longer missions need more breathing room."
	quest.43FA492D62D8EFE2.title: "Upgrade oxygen capacity"
	quest.4427F25EA5E95D82.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Hardened Reactor."
		"Why this matters: This marks the point where power becomes a confident base service rather than a temporary limitation. It supports deeper chemical processing and larger construction projects."
		"Step by step: Upgrade only after the basic system is understood. Stronger hardware amplifies good layout and bad layout alike."
		"Common mistake: A better reactor will not fix items getting stuck in a poorly designed factory."
	]
	quest.4427F25EA5E95D82.quest_subtitle: "Prepare for longer industrial sessions."
	quest.4427F25EA5E95D82.title: "Harden the reactor route"
	quest.4429E8EC4B24CF29.quest_desc: [
		"If an Ender Storage channel behaves strangely, first confirm both endpoints actually use the same frequency and that you did not accidentally repurpose the channel mid-project."
		"If Flux Networks appears weak, inspect the input side, storage behavior, and the remote consumer under load. Wireless transfer cannot create FE that your core grid does not produce."
		"Create Ender Storage improves integration with contraptions, but it does not mean every distant area is automatically chunk-loaded. Design remote systems with that distinction in mind."
		"Troubleshoot local transfer first, then remote transfer. A distant network is rarely easier to fix than the small loop that proves its fundamentals."
	]
	quest.4429E8EC4B24CF29.quest_subtitle: "Check channels, purpose, power flow, and loaded areas."
	quest.4429E8EC4B24CF29.title: "When remote logistics or wireless power feels broken"
	quest.44EAD9852FA704BE.quest_desc: [
		"Centralized storage solves searching. Autocrafting solves repeated recipe assembly. This chapter teaches the difference carefully."
		"Autocrafting is not magic: the network can only craft what patterns describe and what resources are available."
		"Start with simple recipes, verify success, and then expand."
		"A clean autocrafting network begins with a handful of trusted recipes. Build confidence first, then let the system absorb more of your repetitive work."
	]
	quest.44EAD9852FA704BE.quest_subtitle: "A digital network becomes a production assistant."
	quest.44EAD9852FA704BE.title: "From storage to crafting autonomy"
	quest.4654E66862ACC594.quest_desc: [
		"Choose a recipe with ordinary ingredients and a clear output, such as a familiar component you repeatedly craft."
		"Encode it in the Pattern Grid, place it in the Autocrafter, then request the item from the network."
		"If it fails, do not panic. Check ingredient availability, pattern mode, and whether the Autocrafter is connected."
		"After the first recipe succeeds, request it twice more. Repetition proves that the network is reliable rather than merely lucky once."
	]
	quest.4654E66862ACC594.quest_subtitle: "Start with something easy to verify."
	quest.4654E66862ACC594.title: "Encode a simple recipe"
	quest.4672218790CEEA57.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Reach the Mercury phase of the route and obtain Solerium."
		"Why this matters: This quest marks the point where the space route has clearly outgrown first-flight exploration and entered mature mission progression."
		"Step by step: Store it with your other strategic resources and ask what factory upgrades make further collection more repeatable."
		"Common mistake: Rare materials are most useful when they trigger better systems, not when they sit forgotten in a chest."
	]
	quest.4672218790CEEA57.quest_subtitle: "A high-tier space milestone."
	quest.4672218790CEEA57.title: "Secure Solerium"
	quest.46D4F651F87EB207.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Create your first batch of Brass Ingots."
		"Why this matters: Brass unlocks smarter Create logistics, mechanical arms, and the precision-oriented side of the mod. It is the resource that separates basic belts from engineered factories."
		"Step by step: Build or obtain the heat setup required by your recipes, then produce a useful starter batch of brass."
		"Common mistake: Crafting only one or two ingots delays every brass machine that follows."
	]
	quest.46D4F651F87EB207.quest_subtitle: "Brass is the key to precise automation."
	quest.46D4F651F87EB207.title: "Produce Brass"
	quest.46F96D11D58D58CB.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Reactor Solid Access Port."
		"Why this matters: Fuel and waste handling should be planned from the start so the multiblock does not become an awkward manual chore."
		"Place access where routing will remain clear."
		"Put access where logistics can reach it cleanly. Maintenance ports are easiest to love when they remain reachable after the room is finished."
		"Good maintenance beats awkward retrofits, especially in builds that are meant to last many hours."
	]
	quest.46F96D11D58D58CB.quest_subtitle: "Maintenance ports make a machine feel designed."
	quest.46F96D11D58D58CB.title: "Keep fueling accessible"
	quest.47391031470AD45E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the core processing station for Powah recipes."
		"Why this matters: Powah progression depends on energizing recipes. The Orb is not merely decorative; it is the center of that material chain."
		"Step by step: Craft the Orb, place it in a clear area, and leave room for Energizing Rods around it."
		"Common mistake: If you bury the Orb in a cramped machine wall, upgrades become annoying."
	]
	quest.47391031470AD45E.quest_subtitle: "Powah materials begin with this block."
	quest.47391031470AD45E.title: "Craft an Energizing Orb"
	quest.47B0F53A812643AC.quest_desc: [
		"You have now seen that deeper planets are not only sightseeing destinations. Mars, Venus, Mercury, and the Moon each feed a different kind of industrial thinking."
		"This chapter creates pack-owned project items that turn those resources into named plans: habitat design, reactor studies, exotic materials research, and high-energy optics."
		"The items are symbolic by design. They do not replace your own builds; they give those builds a clear Stellar Foundry identity."
		"This chapter intentionally turns raw exploration into project identity. Planetary resources should suggest facilities, not disappear silently into a chest."
	]
	quest.47B0F53A812643AC.quest_subtitle: "RC4 turns destinations into industrial roles."
	quest.47B0F53A812643AC.title: "Planetary materials need a job"
	quest.47C93E0BD7AC99E9.quest_desc: [
		"Refined Storage is the intended approachable digital-storage route. Applied Energistics 2 remains available for players who enjoy a more structured, more technical network system."
		"This chapter does not replace the main storage path. It is a specialization branch for advanced players or for worlds that want AE2 architecture."
		"Beginners should feel free to return later."
		"Treat this branch as an expert alternative rather than mandatory homework. It is strongest when you enjoy its network logic, not when you rush it reluctantly."
	]
	quest.47C93E0BD7AC99E9.quest_subtitle: "More planning, more structure, more control."
	quest.47C93E0BD7AC99E9.title: "Optional expert network: Applied Energistics 2"
	quest.4808EEC3062AE16B.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Create the first piece of protective space gear."
		"Why this matters: The suit is intentionally split into multiple quests so new players do not miss a single armor piece. Space survival is not optional polish."
		"Step by step: Craft the helmet and set it aside in a dedicated mission chest or backpack section."
		"Common mistake: Mixing space gear into random armor storage is an easy way to launch with a missing piece."
	]
	quest.4808EEC3062AE16B.quest_subtitle: "Build the suit piece by piece."
	quest.4808EEC3062AE16B.title: "Craft the Space Suit Helmet"
	quest.484EF643F65C84BC.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Chipped workbench and explore block variations."
		"Why this matters: Technical bases often look better when different wings have distinct materials: workshop, chemistry bay, launch tower, colony shelter. Chipped helps build those palettes."
		"Step by step: Craft one workbench, inspect the available variants, and choose a palette for at least one structure."
		"Common mistake: Using every texture at once makes a base feel less intentional, not more detailed."
	]
	quest.484EF643F65C84BC.quest_subtitle: "Texture variety without abandoning the blocky style."
	quest.484EF643F65C84BC.title: "Use Chipped as a palette tool"
	quest.48585CBF037E633C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the AE2 Controller."
		"Why this matters: AE2 networks reward deliberate channel planning and structured expansion. The Controller marks the moment where this branch becomes a real system."
		"Step by step: Place it only after choosing an area where an AE2 network can grow in a tidy, deliberate shape."
		"Common mistake: Treating AE2 like a copy of Refined Storage hides the design differences that make it interesting."
	]
	quest.48585CBF037E633C.quest_subtitle: "The centerpiece of larger AE2 networks."
	quest.48585CBF037E633C.title: "Craft an ME Controller"
	quest.48E0BA33CD0C3C1A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Place or prepare an Oxygen Distributor for the colony."
		"Why this matters: The distributor symbolizes the shift from expedition to residence. Personal tanks help you visit; infrastructure helps you operate."
		"Step by step: Craft or bring the distributor and place it as part of the habitat plan, not outside as an afterthought."
		"Common mistake: Support machines need placement logic. An oxygen block in the wrong room does not magically solve survival."
	]
	quest.48E0BA33CD0C3C1A.quest_subtitle: "Infrastructure replaces emergency survival."
	quest.48E0BA33CD0C3C1A.title: "Install oxygen support"
	quest.492164768EF65944.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Dissolution Chamber."
		"Why this matters: This is one of the mod’s most important advanced processing blocks and a natural gateway toward more specialized automation."
		"Step by step: Give it a deliberate place in your industry wing and inspect several recipes before treating it as a single-purpose machine."
		"Common mistake: Advanced processing blocks hidden in random corners become hard to revisit when later recipes call for them."
	]
	quest.492164768EF65944.quest_subtitle: "Advanced IF recipes have a centerpiece."
	quest.492164768EF65944.title: "Meet the Dissolution Chamber"
	quest.4B1C4C8E5960FBFD.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the most important early Mekanism machine."
		"Why this matters: The Infuser creates foundational components such as basic circuits and alloys. Those parts unlock nearly every later machine tier."
		"Step by step: Craft it, place it near your FE power, and leave room for a processing row beside it."
		"Common mistake: A machine that needs both an item and an infuse material will not work with only one of them."
	]
	quest.4B1C4C8E5960FBFD.quest_subtitle: "Circuits and alloys start here."
	quest.4B1C4C8E5960FBFD.title: "Craft the Metallurgic Infuser"
	quest.4B674FBB9CD1805D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build or prepare the machine steps necessary to repeat Precision Mechanism production without guesswork."
		"Why this matters: The pack later uses precision components in space-program bridging recipes. A clean workflow now prevents a frustrating bottleneck later."
		"Step by step: Lay out every stage in recipe order, label or visually separate the stages, and verify you can make more than one mechanism."
		"Common mistake: If you cannot explain the order of the sequence, your factory will be hard to debug."
	]
	quest.4B674FBB9CD1805D.quest_subtitle: "Manual crafting once, automation before mass demand."
	quest.4B674FBB9CD1805D.title: "Create a reusable precision workflow"
	quest.4DAB67CF5697C33F.quest_desc: [
		"Prepare a small mission loadout: food, spare blocks, tools, oxygen preparation, and inventory space for discoveries."
		"The exact contents are your choice, but the discipline is not optional. Space exploration feels better when the first trip is a planned expedition."
		"Use a backpack or a clearly labeled chest near the launch area to stage the supplies."
		"Treat the crate as a repeatable template. A good launch kit is something you can rebuild or refill deliberately, not a random emergency backpack."
	]
	quest.4DAB67CF5697C33F.quest_subtitle: "Launch with purpose, not with an empty inventory."
	quest.4DAB67CF5697C33F.title: "Pack a mission crate"
	quest.4F0CD4F0911811D2.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft or obtain a Waystone and place it at your main base."
		"Why this matters: Later you will visit mines, launch sites, and off-world destinations. Clear travel anchors reduce repetitive walking and make large projects feel manageable."
		"Step by step: Place the Waystone somewhere you will not demolish immediately. Name it clearly, such as Main Base."
		"Common mistake: Hiding travel anchors in temporary caves makes navigation harder later."
	]
	quest.4F0CD4F0911811D2.quest_subtitle: "Travel comfort matters in long progression packs."
	quest.4F0CD4F0911811D2.title: "Place a first waypoint"
	quest.4FD30A2E6FA527AB.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Ender Tank."
		"Why this matters: Fluids often become the hidden pain point of late-midgame logistics. A clean dedicated tank frequency can support fuel staging, processing fluids, or off-world utility loops."
		"Step by step: Choose one fluid use case before you place it. Naming the purpose early prevents confusion later."
		"Common mistake: Reusing a tank frequency without thinking can silently contaminate a carefully planned line."
	]
	quest.4FD30A2E6FA527AB.quest_subtitle: "Remote logistics is not only about items."
	quest.4FD30A2E6FA527AB.title: "Craft an Ender Tank"
	quest.501F657FBCC9D7B6.quest_desc: [
		"Create at least two clearly distinct Ender Storage frequencies with explicit purposes. Good examples: 'colony returns' and 'launch supplies', or 'fuel fluids' and 'construction materials'."
		"This checkpoint matters because remote systems become confusing faster than local pipes. You are building infrastructure that future-you must still understand."
		"Keep a sign, book, or obvious color convention near the main transfer wall if you expect the world to last."
		"If you cannot name a channel's purpose immediately, it is probably too vague. Frequency discipline is the remote equivalent of labeling chests."
	]
	quest.501F657FBCC9D7B6.quest_subtitle: "Color codes need purpose, not vibes."
	quest.501F657FBCC9D7B6.title: "Define channel discipline"
	quest.5058132112A675EC.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Learn to inspect recipes and item uses with JEI."
		"Why this matters: A modpack with dozens of machines cannot be memorized from vanilla knowledge. JEI is your recipe manual and your best anti-frustration tool."
		"Step by step: Hover an item, open its recipe, then inspect its uses. Bookmark long crafting chains when a goal involves several components."
		"Common mistake: Crafting from memory instead of checking uses often hides the better automated route."
	]
	quest.5058132112A675EC.quest_subtitle: "Recipes and uses are part of the intended gameplay."
	quest.5058132112A675EC.title: "Use JEI constantly"
	quest.50956B75B6BF3682.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a 1k ME Storage Cell."
		"Why this matters: A small cell is enough to prove the concept. The point is to learn the storage model before chasing huge capacity."
		"Step by step: Insert the cell, move in a few item types, and observe how AE2 represents capacity."
		"Common mistake: AE2 capacity limits work differently from a simple chest count. Pay attention to what the system tells you."
	]
	quest.50956B75B6BF3682.quest_subtitle: "Use the branch for real items."
	quest.50956B75B6BF3682.title: "Prepare a storage cell"
	quest.50C61AD51BB2AB4E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an ME Drive."
		"Why this matters: The drive holds cells, and cells define much of the AE2 capacity philosophy. This branch intentionally uses a more involved storage model."
		"Step by step: Place the drive beside your planned controller network and prepare for terminal access next."
		"Common mistake: A drive without usable cells or access devices cannot replace actual storage."
	]
	quest.50C61AD51BB2AB4E.quest_subtitle: "Storage still needs capacity blocks."
	quest.50C61AD51BB2AB4E.title: "Build an ME Drive"
	quest.50CC024E0CDCBCCE.quest_desc: [
		"Make one compact belt line where an item enters, travels, gets pressed, and exits at a clear collection point."
		"This is the mental model for nearly every later factory: source, motion, machine, destination. The machine choice changes; the logic does not."
		"Keep it simple. A short line that works is more valuable than a sprawling unfinished factory."
		"Let the line process a small stack unattended. If it completes cleanly, you have built your first real machine workflow rather than a decorative contraption."
	]
	quest.50CC024E0CDCBCCE.quest_subtitle: "Input, transport, processing, output."
	quest.50CC024E0CDCBCCE.title: "Build your first automatic line"
	quest.50F5AB0FE426A582.quest_desc: [
		"Check whether power exists, whether it reaches the machine, whether the side configuration allows input, and whether the machine has the exact recipe inputs it needs."
		"If you have an energy buffer, watch whether it fills or drains. That single observation tells you a great deal."
		"A powered-looking cable network is not proof that the target machine is receiving energy."
		"When in doubt, test the machine with a nearby temporary battery or generator. A small controlled experiment separates power issues from recipe issues."
	]
	quest.50F5AB0FE426A582.quest_subtitle: "Energy source, cable, side, internal inventory."
	quest.50F5AB0FE426A582.title: "When an FE machine does not run"
	quest.51235937468C8BE0.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Finish the remaining protective suit pieces."
		"Why this matters: This quest is intentionally explicit: you need the chestplate, leggings, and boots in addition to the helmet."
		"Step by step: Craft each part, keep the set together, and review whether any additional tanks or support items are recommended by JEI or Stellaris tooltips."
		"Common mistake: A visually space-themed helmet does not mean your whole body is protected."
	]
	quest.51235937468C8BE0.quest_subtitle: "Chestplate, leggings, boots."
	quest.51235937468C8BE0.title: "Complete the Space Suit"
	quest.527A677DFFEAB59C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Framed Cubes and inspect how they support custom detailing."
		"Why this matters: Framed Blocks are useful for technical halls, colony walls, windows, and decorative supports where ordinary full blocks feel too blunt."
		"Step by step: Use them sparingly at first in one area of your base to see what they add."
		"Common mistake: Decoration is strongest when it clarifies spaces rather than creating visual noise everywhere."
	]
	quest.527A677DFFEAB59C.quest_subtitle: "Functional shapes with custom visual material."
	quest.527A677DFFEAB59C.title: "Explore framed blocks"
	quest.5333ED8290B4F71F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Basic Flux Storage."
		"Why this matters: Storage inside the Flux layer helps reveal whether your remote system is briefly spiking or permanently underpowered."
		"Step by step: Keep storage somewhere you can inspect during high demand, especially while testing a colony or launch area."
		"Common mistake: A smooth-looking remote network can still be silently draining if you never check buffer behavior."
	]
	quest.5333ED8290B4F71F.quest_subtitle: "Remote networks should have visible headroom."
	quest.5333ED8290B4F71F.title: "Add Flux Storage"
	quest.536D96B0A8ACC384.quest_desc: [
		"Automate a task when it happens often, interrupts a major project, or consumes enough time that a clear machine setup would pay for itself."
		"Do not automate a one-off recipe only because it looks complicated. Do automate recurring circuits, alloys, fuel, food, or expedition preparation if they repeatedly slow you down."
		"The best automation target is the one you resent doing manually."
		"The best automation targets often reveal themselves as repeated frustration. Listen to that friction and let the factory solve it."
	]
	quest.536D96B0A8ACC384.quest_subtitle: "Frequency, pain, and repetition."
	quest.536D96B0A8ACC384.title: "How to decide what to automate next"
	quest.545E3F405E67523F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Turbine Controller."
		"Why this matters: Turbines give the optional reactor route a clear next horizon and distinguish early reactor success from broader plant engineering."
		"You do not need to finish the full turbine immediately to understand the direction."
		"Treat the turbine controller as a signpost toward broader plant engineering, not as pressure to finish the entire next project immediately."
		"You can postpone full turbine construction until the reactor room and its support chain already feel dependable."
	]
	quest.545E3F405E67523F.quest_subtitle: "The branch now points beyond a single block of power."
	quest.545E3F405E67523F.title: "Plan for turbine expansion"
	quest.54A0F25270AC32B0.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Flux Plug."
		"Why this matters: The Plug is the network input. It defines where your generated FE enters the remote energy system."
		"Step by step: Place it near a stable production or buffer node, not in a random cable corner you will forget."
		"Common mistake: If the input side is starved, every remote Flux Point will look weak no matter how well placed."
	]
	quest.54A0F25270AC32B0.quest_subtitle: "Feed energy into the network."
	quest.54A0F25270AC32B0.title: "Build a Flux Plug"
	quest.54B4F0194B650D50.quest_desc: [
		"Use the mod guide, manual, JEI information, or tooltip guidance. Confirm every required block, the overall shape, and any special valve or controller block."
		"Multiblocks often fail because one block is the wrong variant, the footprint is one block off, or the activation tool was not used correctly."
		"Recheck methodically rather than replacing random pieces."
		"Take one screenshot, count layers, or compare the build one slice at a time. Large multiblocks reward boring, careful verification."
	]
	quest.54B4F0194B650D50.quest_subtitle: "Exact block count and orientation matter."
	quest.54B4F0194B650D50.title: "When a multiblock will not form"
	quest.54F6BC0237E51757.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Infused Alloy and treat it as an industrial component."
		"Why this matters: Alloy tiers are used throughout Mekanism upgrades and machine crafting. They are not a one-off curiosity."
		"Step by step: Make a useful batch now. From this point onward, keep circuits and alloys visibly sorted."
		"Common mistake: Mixing finished alloys with random redstone dust in storage often leads to accidental shortages."
	]
	quest.54F6BC0237E51757.quest_subtitle: "The first alloy ladder begins."
	quest.54F6BC0237E51757.title: "Produce Infused Alloy"
	quest.55663CC963D65853.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Rover when off-world movement begins to matter."
		"Why this matters: Planets feel larger than workshops. A rover supports exploration runs, resource scouting, and the sense that you are operating beyond Earth rather than just teleporting for loot."
		"Step by step: Craft it, learn how it behaves, and decide where it belongs in your mission workflow."
		"Common mistake: A mobility tool left unused in a chest is not a solved logistics problem."
	]
	quest.55663CC963D65853.quest_subtitle: "Exploration speed becomes infrastructure."
	quest.55663CC963D65853.title: "Build a Rover"
	quest.55988B878D19DE74.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Hardened Energy Cell."
		"Why this matters: Machine surges and production batches can briefly consume more FE than your generator outputs. Better storage smooths that behavior and makes trends visible."
		"Step by step: Place the cell where you can inspect it during a high-load operation."
		"Common mistake: A grid with no visible buffer gives you fewer clues when throughput drops."
	]
	quest.55988B878D19DE74.quest_subtitle: "Buffers make demand spikes manageable."
	quest.55988B878D19DE74.title: "Upgrade energy storage"
	quest.55BD192AC4CBDE48.quest_desc: [
		"The Mission Manifest is a thematic checkpoint. It marks the moment where your base becomes a deliberate space program rather than a pile of unrelated machines."
		"Craft it and use this moment to review your launch area, food, gear, storage, power, and return plan."
		"A good first mission is short, prepared, and repeatable."
		"The next chapters assume you are launching as an engineer with a plan, not as an explorer hoping that one inventory of random supplies will be enough."
	]
	quest.55BD192AC4CBDE48.quest_subtitle: "Plan before you leave Earth."
	quest.55BD192AC4CBDE48.title: "Write a Mission Manifest"
	quest.565FDC85AA3187DF.quest_desc: [
		"Precision Mechanisms are crafted through a repeated Create-style processing sequence. They are a perfect example of a recipe that deserves automation."
		"Use JEI to examine the sequence carefully before building. Note every intermediate pass and every required tool or machine."
		"Your goal here is to craft the mechanism once and understand the chain. A later quest asks you to improve the workflow."
		"If the sequence looks intimidating, read it from left to right as repeated stations. Create automation becomes simpler when every pass has one clear job."
	]
	quest.565FDC85AA3187DF.quest_subtitle: "Sequenced assembly is a core Create lesson."
	quest.565FDC85AA3187DF.title: "Meet precision mechanisms"
	quest.56628F96AAA0AC43.quest_desc: [
		"Add at least one machine or automated process that gives the outpost a purpose: ore pre-processing, resource staging, oxygen support, fuel support, or construction material handling."
		"The exact solution depends on your chosen planet and playstyle, but it should reduce a recurring burden."
		"A colony becomes meaningful when it changes your workflow."
		"Even a small processing chain makes the location meaningful. A colony that changes one repetitive workflow has already earned its footprint."
	]
	quest.56628F96AAA0AC43.quest_subtitle: "The colony should do something useful."
	quest.56628F96AAA0AC43.title: "Create a local processing step"
	quest.56B591980E23EB91.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Oxygen Sealer and study its role."
		"Why this matters: This is one of the most valuable conceptual blocks in the addon because it connects construction quality with environmental survival."
		"Step by step: Craft it, then read its behavior before placing it in a rushed outpost. Sealed-volume logic deserves attention."
		"Common mistake: A room that looks closed to you may not be closed to the machine."
	]
	quest.56B591980E23EB91.quest_subtitle: "Rooms can become survival systems."
	quest.56B591980E23EB91.title: "Understand Oxygen Sealers"
	quest.57053640D31D931F.quest_desc: [
		"Design your grid so one short interruption does not instantly collapse all important production. You can use energy buffers, staged generators, controlled demand, or clear priority zones."
		"Test the idea by observing how the base behaves under load or temporary generation interruption."
		"A mature factory is not only fast. It is stable."
		"Test the backup once by simulating a problem: empty a buffer, stop a generator, or isolate a branch. Resilience should be proven, not assumed."
	]
	quest.57053640D31D931F.quest_subtitle: "Resilience is a mark of maturity."
	quest.57053640D31D931F.title: "Build a backup power strategy"
	quest.5754F0345148B4C4.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Establish a safe place to work before you dive into modded systems."
		"Why this matters: Your early machines will be easier to expand if they are not jammed into a panic shelter or scattered across the landscape."
		"Step by step: Collect logs, cobblestone, coal or charcoal, and create a lit starter room with crafting, furnaces, and room for expansion."
		"Common mistake: A tiny cave base with no layout usually turns into a painful rebuild later."
		"Iron Furnaces is also present as a practical optional upgrade path when ordinary smelting starts to feel too slow."
	]
	quest.5754F0345148B4C4.quest_subtitle: "The industrial age still starts with vanilla survival."
	quest.5754F0345148B4C4.title: "Secure wood, stone, and shelter"
	quest.577DAC39E9CF2F5C.quest_desc: [
		"Do not launch because the rocket exists. Launch when the mission exists: fuel, suit, oxygen, staging supplies, destination intent, and a recovery or return plan."
		"Space is exciting, but the modpack is designed to reward preparation."
		"If you feel uncertain, reread the fuel and first-launch chapters."
		"An aborted launch preparation is a success if it catches a missing supply before liftoff. Good engineering prevents dramatic mistakes."
	]
	quest.577DAC39E9CF2F5C.quest_subtitle: "Return to the checklist."
	quest.577DAC39E9CF2F5C.title: "When a rocket mission feels unsafe"
	quest.584000DBBD035263.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce a batch of Advanced Control Circuits."
		"Why this matters: These parts signal that the factory is moving beyond first machines. They appear in upgrades, processing blocks, and technical projects throughout the midgame."
		"Step by step: Make at least four and store them with your high-grade components."
		"Common mistake: If advanced circuits feel painful, improve alloy and basic circuit production before pushing forward."
	]
	quest.584000DBBD035263.quest_subtitle: "A true second tier of electronics."
	quest.584000DBBD035263.title: "Craft Advanced Control Circuits"
	quest.595673EDF41CEE78.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Explore Applied Mekanistics with a chemical storage or integration component."
		"Why this matters: This addon exists because Mekanism’s gases and chemicals matter in Stellar Foundry. It gives AE2-focused players a way to integrate that complexity elegantly."
		"Step by step: Craft the entry-level chemical storage cell and inspect its role before designing a network around it."
		"Common mistake: Advanced integration is powerful, but only when you understand both systems separately first."
	]
	quest.595673EDF41CEE78.quest_subtitle: "Optional networks can still connect to the pack core."
	quest.595673EDF41CEE78.title: "Applied Mekanistics bridge"
	quest.59AF7F3CE55CEFCC.quest_desc: [
		"Write a clear mental policy for colony operations: what you carry from Earth, what is produced locally, what returns home, and how emergencies are handled."
		"Then adjust one colony to follow that policy."
		"This turns colonies from scenic outposts into a real interplanetary system."
		"A supply doctrine matters because it prevents colonies from becoming forgotten boxes of mixed loot. Policy turns remote building into a system."
	]
	quest.59AF7F3CE55CEFCC.quest_subtitle: "Define what colonies receive and what they produce."
	quest.59AF7F3CE55CEFCC.title: "Create a permanent colony supply doctrine"
	quest.5AA984F61D18A62D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Disk Drive and attach it to the network."
		"Why this matters: The Drive holds storage disks. Separating access, control, and capacity teaches you how the network can later scale cleanly."
		"Step by step: Place the drive adjacent or cable-connected to the controller network, then prepare a small disk."
		"Common mistake: The Grid may open correctly while still showing no capacity if storage was never added."
	]
	quest.5AA984F61D18A62D.quest_subtitle: "A network without storage cannot hold anything."
	quest.5AA984F61D18A62D.title: "Add a Disk Drive"
	quest.5AAB2C47C731DFC7.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Powah Reactor."
		"Why this matters: Reactors introduce a more intentional power plant than your earliest generators. They belong in a utility area with room for storage, cables, and future upgrades."
		"Step by step: Craft one and plan its placement before setting it down permanently."
		"Common mistake: Power generation hidden in a cramped corner becomes a problem when the grid needs debugging."
	]
	quest.5AAB2C47C731DFC7.quest_subtitle: "A real base grid deserves a serious generator."
	quest.5AAB2C47C731DFC7.title: "Build a Basic Reactor"
	quest.5AB64DD89FF7CCAF.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an LV Capacitor and Copper Wire Coil."
		"Why this matters: Immersive Engineering power presentation is visually distinct from enclosed tech blocks. It can make industrial yards and themed utility rooms feel more believable."
		"Step by step: Craft the basic components and inspect safe connection logic before placing a large visible wire network."
		"Common mistake: A decorative wire grid still needs real power logic if you expect it to run machines."
	]
	quest.5AB64DD89FF7CCAF.quest_subtitle: "A different style of energy presentation."
	quest.5AB64DD89FF7CCAF.title: "Build low-voltage storage and wiring"
	quest.5AD2625B6D3B34D9.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a useful drawer solution for bulk items."
		"Why this matters: Storage Drawers are excellent for high-volume resources. They make it obvious when a resource is abundant or nearly empty."
		"Step by step: Use drawers for materials you repeatedly gather or process. Compacting drawers are especially helpful for ingot, nugget, and block forms."
		"Common mistake: Drawers are not automatically better for every item. Use them where visibility and volume matter."
	]
	quest.5AD2625B6D3B34D9.quest_subtitle: "Cobblestone and ores deserve predictable homes."
	quest.5AD2625B6D3B34D9.title: "Use drawers for bulk materials"
	quest.5B0CEFC6B2200E6B.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Reactor Controller."
		"Why this matters: The controller anchors the reactor and gives the structure its visible point of operation."
		"Place it where the reactor room remains serviceable later."
		"Place the controller toward a service corridor or control face so the machine reads like an operated plant rather than a hidden box."
		"A clear front side helps future troubleshooting and gives the power room stronger visual identity."
	]
	quest.5B0CEFC6B2200E6B.quest_subtitle: "Every serious machine needs a control face."
	quest.5B0CEFC6B2200E6B.title: "Add a Reactor Controller"
	quest.5B86388CB9176209.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Reprocessor Controller."
		"Why this matters: Reprocessing gives the chapter a fitting final industrial endpoint and shows that reactor projects create their own supporting infrastructure."
		"Claim the patch when the reactor route feels like a complete optional engineering system."
		"Keep the reactor area paired with the processing or maintenance logic that supports it so the plant feels self-contained."
		"Closing this chapter means the reactor route has become a coherent optional power program, not a loose pile of advanced blocks."
	]
	quest.5B86388CB9176209.quest_subtitle: "A power plant is strongest when its support chain exists too."
	quest.5B86388CB9176209.title: "Close the reactor engineering branch"
	quest.5C90533EB7AF9E5D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Laser Wrench."
		"Why this matters: This final tool symbolizes that the Actually Additions branch is no longer just unlocked; it is maintainable and configurable."
		"Claim the patch when the lab feels like a usable optional system."
		"Review whether the Reconstructor, energy handling, relay routing, and Empowerer area now feel like one coherent optional lab."
		"The branch is complete when it is usable and legible, not merely when every reward has been claimed."
	]
	quest.5C90533EB7AF9E5D.quest_subtitle: "A finished optional lab should be easy to adjust."
	quest.5C90533EB7AF9E5D.title: "Close the reconstruction branch"
	quest.5DEC277BFF7BA5F3.quest_desc: [
		"You now own a rocket, but a safe mission still needs fuel production, fuel handling, and a final readiness check."
		"This chapter prevents a common modpack failure: crafting the exciting object first, then discovering that the operational chain behind it is missing."
		"Treat the launchpad as a system, not as a display stand."
		"Fuel logistics is the difference between a one-time achievement and a repeatable space program. This chapter exists to remove that future pain."
	]
	quest.5DEC277BFF7BA5F3.quest_subtitle: "Fuel and launch support decide whether it flies."
	quest.5DEC277BFF7BA5F3.title: "A rocket is not a mission yet"
	quest.5E4CB3089BDA4A20.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Venus Materials Matrix."
		"Why this matters: Neptunium, Corronium, PneumaticCraft electronics, and pressure-era sealing now converge in one recipe."
		"Venus becomes the pack's materials-science destination instead of only a place where you grab two ingots and leave."
		"Store the Matrix beside Venus materials or pressure-era machinery. Its placement can help communicate the pack's materials-science storyline."
	]
	quest.5E4CB3089BDA4A20.quest_subtitle: "Exotic planetary metals feed advanced research."
	quest.5E4CB3089BDA4A20.title: "Assemble a Venus Materials Matrix"
	quest.5ED949DDC2A31105.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Ender Pouch."
		"Why this matters: The pouch lets you access a chosen Ender Storage frequency while exploring or building. For a space pack, that is perfect for return samples, emergency supplies, and construction staging."
		"Step by step: Bind it to a frequency you can explain in one sentence. If the channel has no name in your head, it will not stay organized."
		"Common mistake: Treating a pouch as an infinite junk drawer creates the same clutter problem in a different format."
	]
	quest.5ED949DDC2A31105.quest_subtitle: "Field access turns channels into mission tools."
	quest.5ED949DDC2A31105.title: "Carry an Ender Pouch"
	quest.5F6BEC195CB1FD40.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the Stellaris Rocket. This is not the end of the pack; it is the point where your terrestrial factory becomes a launch-capable civilization."
		"Before the first flight, verify the full suit, oxygen preparation, fuel plan, inventory space, and a return strategy."
		"A prepared launch is satisfying. A rushed launch is usually a recovery mission."
		"After crafting the rocket, leave it staged near the pad and treat the area like a real launch complex. Clear staging helps reveal missing support steps."
	]
	quest.5F6BEC195CB1FD40.quest_subtitle: "The pack’s first major headline milestone."
	quest.5F6BEC195CB1FD40.title: "Assemble the first Rocket"
	quest.608C75344A191062.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Empty Blaze Burner and understand why it matters."
		"Why this matters: Several important Create recipes require heat. The burner is the stepping stone from simple motion to serious material processing."
		"Step by step: Craft it now, then check JEI and the upcoming brass quests so you know exactly what it will be used for."
		"Common mistake: Do not assume every mixed recipe needs heat. JEI tells you which ones do."
	]
	quest.608C75344A191062.quest_subtitle: "Heated processing changes what is possible."
	quest.608C75344A191062.title: "Prepare a Blaze Burner"
	quest.60AC74B0EC53242E.quest_desc: [
		"Construct the first permanent structure of your off-world outpost. It should be clearly enclosed, lit, and organized enough that you can return to it later without rebuilding from scratch."
		"Use Stellaris or Create Space environmental systems where appropriate for your chosen route."
		"The goal is not decoration first. The goal is a functional base that can later become beautiful."
		"Return to the habitat later and ask whether it still feels safe when you arrive in a hurry. Good outposts communicate their purpose immediately."
	]
	quest.60AC74B0EC53242E.quest_subtitle: "A colony begins with a safe room."
	quest.60AC74B0EC53242E.title: "Build a sealed or protected habitat"
	quest.615A2B49E3D8A064.quest_desc: [
		"Verify that the Controller is powered. Then confirm the Grid is connected to the same network. Next, check whether a Drive contains a storage disk or whether External Storage targets are actually connected."
		"If the interface opens but no capacity exists, the issue is usually storage, not the Grid."
		"Solve the network from center outward."
		"Start with the smallest possible working network in your mind: one controller, one access block, one storage source. Then compare your real base against it."
	]
	quest.615A2B49E3D8A064.quest_subtitle: "Controller power, drive capacity, connections."
	quest.615A2B49E3D8A064.title: "When Refined Storage appears empty or offline"
	quest.617B7EAC29AE44F5.quest_desc: [
		"The questbook is intentionally divided into five main route groups. Work through them from Main Route 1/5 to Main Route 5/5."
		"Mission Control is the progress tracker above them: it turns key milestone patches into visible tier goals and reward claims."
		"Optional Systems and Worldbuilding contains side branches that make a base richer, but they are not required to understand the core route."
		"Reference and Mastery is for troubleshooting, planning reminders, and late self-directed goals. If you feel lost, return there, Mission Control, or to this roadmap."
	]
	quest.617B7EAC29AE44F5.quest_subtitle: "Five main phases, optional branches, one clear route."
	quest.617B7EAC29AE44F5.title: "Read the Progression Map"
	quest.620E4A1A12A6684A.quest_desc: [
		"Complete this checkpoint when your world has: at least one purposeful Ender Storage channel, a proven remote Flux power route, and a clear idea for how resources or support will reach future outposts."
		"This chapter is not asking for every base to be wireless. It is asking for remote infrastructure to be a design choice rather than an emergency reaction."
		"From here, colonies should feel like extensions of your industrial program instead of isolated survival boxes."
		"If this chapter works, future colonies will feel supported by the home factory instead of abandoned at the edge of the progression."
	]
	quest.620E4A1A12A6684A.quest_subtitle: "Your future colonies now have a backbone."
	quest.620E4A1A12A6684A.title: "Remote logistics charter"
	quest.62101C96F3602884.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Acquire an Ice Shard from the early off-world loop."
		"Why this matters: Space progression should teach environmental harvesting and not only ore mining. Ice and oxygen-related materials often matter for survivability and base planning."
		"Step by step: Bring back at least one shard and inspect its JEI uses before throwing it into storage."
		"Common mistake: Ignoring non-metal resources can quietly block later recipes."
	]
	quest.62101C96F3602884.quest_subtitle: "Not every valuable space resource is a metal."
	quest.62101C96F3602884.title: "Collect an Ice Shard"
	quest.623DF0727D7B84EA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Rocket Flight Computer."
		"Why this matters: This is the capstone bridge item of the pre-launch factory. It represents a combined result of Create precision, Mekanism control, and pressure-era materials."
		"Step by step: Prepare every part in advance, then craft the final component cleanly through JEI."
		"Common mistake: If the recipe tree feels too long, it is revealing which previous component you never automated."
	]
	quest.623DF0727D7B84EA.quest_subtitle: "A launch should have a real control core."
	quest.623DF0727D7B84EA.title: "Assemble a Rocket Flight Computer"
	quest.625187D99B63DC54.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Create a dedicated room or platform for the first technical systems."
		"Why this matters: Create contraptions and later cable networks need clear routing. A rectangle with enough walking space is better than an overdecorated cramped bunker."
		"Step by step: Reserve at least one medium-sized area for Create, one wall for storage, and a side for furnaces or early power blocks."
		"Common mistake: You can decorate later. At this stage, readable layout beats visual perfection."
	]
	quest.625187D99B63DC54.quest_subtitle: "Leave space for belts, shafts, and power cables."
	quest.625187D99B63DC54.title: "Build a clean starter workshop"
	quest.626D1DAA5302D803.quest_desc: [
		"Stellar Foundry is not only about machines. Bases, launchpads, control rooms, warehouses, and colonies become more memorable when the architecture reinforces the theme."
		"This chapter gathers fitting building tools and asks you to use them in service of clarity and identity."
		"Build beautifully, but never at the cost of readability."
		"Chisels and Bits belongs here as a decorative precision tool for launch pads, laboratories, and colony details."
	]
	quest.626D1DAA5302D803.quest_subtitle: "A top-tier factory deserves readable architecture."
	quest.626D1DAA5302D803.title: "Optional: make the world look like the progression feels"
	quest.6284E6FE7EDED9A3.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Reinforced Alloy."
		"Why this matters: Mekanism intentionally layers its materials. Each tier is a signal that your earlier input chain must become more repeatable."
		"Step by step: Produce a useful reserve and take note of what intermediate material your factory now consumes most often."
		"Common mistake: Trying to bypass the alloy ladder with tiny manual batches creates chronic bottlenecks."
	]
	quest.6284E6FE7EDED9A3.quest_subtitle: "The alloy ladder continues."
	quest.6284E6FE7EDED9A3.title: "Produce Reinforced Alloy"
	quest.62EC927E683B3408.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Cryogenic Tank."
		"Why this matters: Space-resource processing often introduces special fluids. A dedicated tank keeps this addon readable and signals that you are entering a more specialized engineering layer."
		"Step by step: Place the tank near the relevant machines and keep space around it for future piping or transport."
		"Common mistake: Do not scatter special-fluid storage across the base without labels or layout logic."
	]
	quest.62EC927E683B3408.quest_subtitle: "Cold liquids need intentional storage."
	quest.62EC927E683B3408.title: "Set up cryogenic handling"
	quest.63D6A44DCCA6587B.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Produce basic rocket structure pieces for the Create route."
		"Why this matters: Casing and engine parts are where the addon’s concept becomes visually clear. You are preparing a contraption capable of launch."
		"Step by step: Craft several Rocket Casings and a Small Rocket Engine, then review the addon’s assembly guidance carefully."
		"Common mistake: Building by appearance instead of the addon’s intended structure often causes failed first attempts."
	]
	quest.63D6A44DCCA6587B.quest_subtitle: "The machine becomes a vehicle."
	quest.63D6A44DCCA6587B.title: "Craft casing and a small engine"
	quest.63E2799ECDD531DA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build one small, valid Create: Creating Space rocket prototype using the parts and machines from this chapter."
		"Why this matters: The addon becomes understandable when the components stop being isolated recipe icons and begin acting like a vehicle project."
		"Step by step: Use the addon guidance from the Rocket Engineering Table, place the required controls, casing, engine, and supporting structure, then verify that the design is recognized as a proper rocket setup."
		"Common mistake: Building a rocket-shaped statue is not the same as building the addon's valid rocket structure. Follow the table and in-game guidance carefully."
	]
	quest.63E2799ECDD531DA.quest_subtitle: "Turn individual parts into a real engineering experiment."
	quest.63E2799ECDD531DA.title: "Assemble a first Create-route rocket prototype"
	quest.6418E541090F1EBA.quest_desc: [
		"Physical storage is still useful, but the machine era creates too many parts to manage entirely by barrels and drawers."
		"Refined Storage becomes your base brain: searchable items, centralized access, simple routing, and later autocrafting."
		"This chapter starts small. Build a functional network before you chase huge disks or fancy wireless access."
		"Bulk drawers can still remain useful beside a digital network. The goal is not to delete physical storage, but to make daily access and crafting calmer."
	]
	quest.6418E541090F1EBA.quest_subtitle: "Your component count is about to explode."
	quest.6418E541090F1EBA.title: "Why digital storage now?"
	quest.6591C27BF478EF07.quest_desc: [
		"Review the entire first-launch chain and remove the worst remaining manual bottleneck. A repeat mission should be far easier than the first."
		"This may mean improving fuel handling, staging oxygen gear, autocrafting bridge components, or organizing launch inventory."
		"The standard is simple: after one mission, preparing the next one should feel routine rather than chaotic."
		"A good test is to prepare for a second launch immediately after returning from one. If that feels routine, your supply chain has matured."
	]
	quest.6591C27BF478EF07.quest_subtitle: "Fuel, mission components, and staging should recover cleanly."
	quest.6591C27BF478EF07.title: "Build repeatable launch supply"
	quest.66229CDF985E1A1C.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build a working Windmill Bearing setup as an optional upgrade beyond the first Water Wheel."
		"Why this matters: Windmills teach a second Create concept that beginners often miss: some machines only work after a structure is assembled into a contraption."
		"Step by step: Craft a Windmill Bearing and sail frames, attach a simple rotor shape, activate the bearing, and confirm that it actually spins."
		"Common mistake: Placed sails are not power by themselves. The bearing must assemble a valid moving structure before it produces rotation."
	]
	quest.66229CDF985E1A1C.quest_subtitle: "A larger passive Create power source teaches structure assembly."
	quest.66229CDF985E1A1C.title: "Optional upgrade: build a Windmill"
	quest.669BB147C905C48F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Plant Gatherer."
		"Why this matters: A sower without collection is only half an automation system. The Gatherer converts field growth into storage-ready output."
		"Step by step: Pair it with the Sower, provide power, and plan item extraction from the machine."
		"Common mistake: If the Gatherer fills up, the farm is not fully automated yet."
	]
	quest.669BB147C905C48F.quest_subtitle: "Plant Gatherer closes the first agricultural loop."
	quest.669BB147C905C48F.title: "Automate crop harvesting"
	quest.66ADB9FE5D06B744.quest_desc: [
		"Create: Creating Space offers a second kind of space fantasy: instead of only assembling a defined rocket recipe, you engineer a Create-flavored launch workflow with specialized machines and rocket structure blocks."
		"This chapter is optional for main progression, but it fits the pack identity so well that it is strongly recommended once you understand both Create and the basic Stellaris route."
		"Use it as an engineering side project, not as a replacement for learning the main space program."
		"Expect experimentation. This branch rewards players who enjoy understanding moving parts, build space, and the visual engineering of a launch vehicle."
	]
	quest.66ADB9FE5D06B744.quest_subtitle: "Optional, thematic, and highly recommended."
	quest.66ADB9FE5D06B744.title: "Alternative route: Create-style rocketry"
	quest.66C7136C6AB63DF0.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Importer and Exporter."
		"Why this matters: These blocks connect machine workflows to your digital storage. They are perfect for simple, clear cases where the network should stock or collect items."
		"Step by step: Use them on one small processing step, then verify you understand which side inserts and which side extracts."
		"Common mistake: Swapping import and export roles is one of the most common early network mistakes."
	]
	quest.66C7136C6AB63DF0.quest_subtitle: "Networks become useful when they touch machines."
	quest.66C7136C6AB63DF0.title: "Use Refined Storage import and export"
	quest.66CDC33D387F1FD4.quest_desc: [
		"After your first excursion, write the lessons into your base plan: which supplies ran short, what resources deserve automation, and what launch support needs improvement."
		"This is the moment where the pack pivots from a single rocket toward a repeating space program."
		"Complete the checkmark only after you have reviewed your actual experience."
		"Before scheduling another mission, note which supply ran low first and which step felt awkward. That observation should shape your next automation project."
	]
	quest.66CDC33D387F1FD4.quest_subtitle: "What did space reveal your factory still lacks?"
	quest.66CDC33D387F1FD4.title: "First expedition review"
	quest.6803438338D5DC75.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft belt connectors and prepare a short transport line."
		"Why this matters: Belts turn isolated machines into production lines. The moment items move themselves, Create becomes much more than a crafting helper."
		"Step by step: Place two shafts, connect them with a belt, and test item movement from one end to the other."
		"Common mistake: Belts require correct shaft spacing and alignment."
	]
	quest.6803438338D5DC75.quest_subtitle: "Item movement is the first taste of automation."
	quest.6803438338D5DC75.title: "Unlock belts"
	quest.68DF67FA365635D3.quest_desc: [
		"Create Ender Storage is included because it makes the pack feel more intentional: Create contraptions can access Ender Storage inventories rather than every remote transfer being a static box and pipe problem."
		"Build or plan one small use case. A contraption-fed supply buffer, station loading line, or factory endpoint connected to a matching Ender Storage frequency all fit the spirit."
		"Important: this integration does not magically chunk-load distant areas. Remote logistics still deserves sane world design."
		"Keep one simple demonstration build even after expanding. A small readable example makes future troubleshooting much faster."
	]
	quest.68DF67FA365635D3.quest_subtitle: "Contraptions can now participate in remote logistics."
	quest.68DF67FA365635D3.title: "Bridge Create with Ender Storage"
	quest.6933B08DCD35AA62.quest_desc: [
		"Decide how materials move conceptually between your main base, launch area, and off-world outposts. You might use prepared mission kits, remote power, local refinement, or dedicated staging warehouses."
		"The pack does not force a single answer. It asks for a deliberate answer."
		"Complete this quest only when you can explain your multi-base logistics philosophy in one or two sentences."
		"Write the philosophy on a sign, in a book, or as a clear mental standard. Consistent logistics decisions make large worlds feel professional."
	]
	quest.6933B08DCD35AA62.quest_subtitle: "Earth and colonies should feel connected by planning."
	quest.6933B08DCD35AA62.title: "Design a multi-base logistics philosophy"
	quest.69B12D1AD77851DA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Basic Universal Cables and connect a small Mekanism processing row."
		"Why this matters: Cables are not exciting, but cable discipline keeps factories maintainable. Straight runs, clean junctions, and accessible machines matter."
		"Step by step: Connect Infuser, Enrichment Chamber, and Crusher in a way you can understand at a glance."
		"Common mistake: Cable spaghetti feels fast for five minutes and slow for the next ten hours."
	]
	quest.69B12D1AD77851DA.quest_subtitle: "Build a readable power backbone."
	quest.69B12D1AD77851DA.title: "Lay Universal Cables"
	quest.69D02808D5419C7C.quest_desc: [
		"Create a small kitchen, briefing room, bedroom, greenhouse corner, or observation deck. It does not need to be large; it needs to have a clear purpose."
		"This quest is deliberately open because atmosphere is personal. The pack only asks that your world contain at least one space built for comfort rather than throughput."
		"Long-term worlds deserve places where nothing is being smelted."
		"The more technical the base becomes, the more valuable a human-scale room feels. Comfort design is what keeps a long world memorable."
	]
	quest.69D02808D5419C7C.quest_subtitle: "A base should feel inhabited."
	quest.69D02808D5419C7C.title: "Build one room that exists for players, not machines"
	quest.69E7AC04EC058994.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Air Liquefier."
		"Why this matters: This machine reinforces the idea that a space program depends on atmospheric, fluid, and gas preparation, not only metal crafting."
		"Step by step: Set it up near your Create Space engineering area and read its JEI uses or tooltip before integrating it."
		"Common mistake: A machine can be correctly crafted and still seem mysterious if you never inspect its output role."
	]
	quest.69E7AC04EC058994.quest_subtitle: "The Air Liquefier makes the route feel alive."
	quest.69E7AC04EC058994.title: "Extract from the air"
	quest.6A2A828B70643C3A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Flux Dust."
		"Why this matters: Flux Networks deserves a dedicated onboarding step rather than appearing as a mystery late-game block. Flux Dust begins the path toward readable wireless energy lanes."
		"Step by step: Produce the dust, inspect its uses in JEI, and understand that Flux parts are not a replacement for power generation. They are a routing layer."
		"Common mistake: Remote power transfer cannot fix a generator that is already underbuilt."
	]
	quest.6A2A828B70643C3A.quest_subtitle: "Wireless FE starts with its own material line."
	quest.6A2A828B70643C3A.title: "Begin Flux Networks"
	quest.6B1621EBF7396359.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Crusher and learn to compare processing recipes."
		"Why this matters: Not every machine exists to replace another. The Crusher opens different recipes and later pairs naturally with transporters or digital routing."
		"Step by step: Place it in the same Mekanism area and check several JEI uses before moving on."
		"Common mistake: Assuming every machine doubles ore is a common misunderstanding. Always check the actual recipe."
	]
	quest.6B1621EBF7396359.quest_subtitle: "Processing chains benefit from role clarity."
	quest.6B1621EBF7396359.title: "Add a Crusher"
	quest.6B99B9372D55ADE7.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Interplanetary Industry Charter."
		"Why this matters: The charter consumes all four planetary project items together with your launch-era planning objects. It makes the pack's space arc feel like one designed industrial program."
		"From here, the colony chapter asks you to turn that plan into permanent infrastructure rather than another quick resource raid."
		"Once crafted, treat the Charter as the bridge between exploration and civilization. The next phase asks you to make those plans tangible."
	]
	quest.6B99B9372D55ADE7.quest_subtitle: "Every major destination now has a role."
	quest.6B99B9372D55ADE7.title: "Issue the Interplanetary Industry Charter"
	quest.6C5E18ADE3FB441A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Nuclear Fuel."
		"Why this matters: Nuclear fuel gives the Create electrical branch an unmistakable late-stage horizon and a strong reason to keep exploring the addon."
		"Claim the patch once the branch feels integrated into your factory language."
		"Do not treat the capstone as an isolated exotic recipe. It should feel like the endpoint of a coherent electrical side progression."
		"Use it to connect this branch back to the broader endgame language of high-energy industry and long-term factory ambition."
	]
	quest.6C5E18ADE3FB441A.quest_subtitle: "The optional electrical route now has a real capstone."
	quest.6C5E18ADE3FB441A.title: "Reach the nuclear electrical horizon"
	quest.6CACC6EC7AFCEA8E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Chemical Oxidizer."
		"Why this matters: The oxidizer expands the chemical side of Mekanism and prepares you for more involved resource and material chains."
		"Step by step: Place it in the same chemistry zone and compare its JEI recipe categories with those of the Electrolytic Separator."
		"Common mistake: Learning what each machine category produces is faster than memorizing isolated recipes."
	]
	quest.6CACC6EC7AFCEA8E.quest_subtitle: "Chemical recipes need dedicated transformations."
	quest.6CACC6EC7AFCEA8E.title: "Add a Chemical Oxidizer"
	quest.6D77C2DEFD19A839.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Lunar Habitat Survey."
		"Why this matters: Moon resources, oxygen planning, and launch paperwork now combine into a colony-planning object instead of staying as unrelated checklist parts."
		"Use it as a sign that your first off-world foothold has moved from tourism to design."
		"Pair the survey with a real habitat sketch, staging shelf, or labeled colony crate so the planning object visibly changes how you approach the Moon."
	]
	quest.6D77C2DEFD19A839.quest_subtitle: "The Moon becomes more than a first landing."
	quest.6D77C2DEFD19A839.title: "Draft a Lunar Habitat Survey"
	quest.6D8FBCE6D7EF5C29.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Reactor Fuel Rod."
		"Why this matters: Fuel rods are the functional heart of the reactor shape and make internal layout choices meaningful."
		"Build small first so you can understand the multiblock before scaling."
		"Plan rod count and internal spacing before final casing placement. The inside of the multiblock is where engineering decisions become physical."
		"Internal layout influences how the reactor feels to build, inspect, and expand later."
	]
	quest.6D8FBCE6D7EF5C29.quest_subtitle: "Internal layout is part of the engineering."
	quest.6D8FBCE6D7EF5C29.title: "Prepare the Fuel Rod core"
	quest.6DDE9E464DB56CE5.quest_desc: [
		"Complete this quest when the outpost has: a permanent structure, environmental thought, power plan, storage plan, and at least one useful work function."
		"That standard is intentionally clear but not overly prescriptive. A good colony should reflect your world while still meeting real operational needs."
		"This is one of the most important identity milestones in Stellar Foundry."
		"If all five needs are met and the outpost still reads clearly, you have built a colony rather than a temporary survival bunker."
	]
	quest.6DDE9E464DB56CE5.quest_subtitle: "You now own a second industrial foothold."
	quest.6DDE9E464DB56CE5.title: "Colony charter"
	quest.6E7E4F48E45F942D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the XNet Controller as an optional next-level logistics tool."
		"Why this matters: XNet is excellent for compact, configurable transport when many nearby machines need item, fluid, or energy logic. It is more powerful, but also more abstract."
		"Step by step: Craft the Controller now and inspect how channels and connectors are organized. Use it after the simpler tools make sense."
		"Common mistake: Do not use complexity to avoid learning the basic flow of items."
	]
	quest.6E7E4F48E45F942D.quest_subtitle: "Compact channel networks reward planning."
	quest.6E7E4F48E45F942D.title: "Introduce XNet only when networks grow"
	quest.6ED3D10FCB635E1A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the first dedicated space-program component."
		"Why this matters: This item should feel like a product of your factory, not a vanilla trinket. It combines the idea of mechanical precision and advanced control."
		"Step by step: Check JEI for the updated recipe, gather its component types from your existing systems, and craft one."
		"Common mistake: If you are crafting every prerequisite manually from scratch, improve the earlier factory loops first."
	]
	quest.6ED3D10FCB635E1A.quest_subtitle: "Precision engineering meets electronic control."
	quest.6ED3D10FCB635E1A.title: "Build an Orbital Guidance Chip"
	quest.6FC25A84ACA93FBC.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Brass Funnel and inspect how filters change item flow."
		"Why this matters: A production line becomes reliable when it receives the right inputs and exports the right outputs. Funnels are one of the simplest tools for that control."
		"Step by step: Place a funnel on an inventory or belt, apply a filter if useful, and observe how it changes item movement."
		"Common mistake: Unfiltered outputs can clog later machines with the wrong item."
	]
	quest.6FC25A84ACA93FBC.quest_subtitle: "Logistics should not rely on manual tossing."
	quest.6FC25A84ACA93FBC.title: "Use funnels for controlled input and output"
	quest.6FE03602A9C535F9.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Run a small manual pressing workflow until you understand input, operation, and output."
		"Why this matters: Automation works best when you first understand the manual version. This teaches what the machine expects before belts and filters hide the details."
		"Step by step: Place input on the Depot, wait for the press cycle, and collect the result. Repeat enough times that the behavior feels obvious."
		"Common mistake: If a machine seems broken, verify power, position, and recipe before assuming a mod issue."
	]
	quest.6FE03602A9C535F9.quest_subtitle: "Do not build machines as museum pieces."
	quest.6FE03602A9C535F9.title: "Use Create processing deliberately"
	quest.701EC555B9672189.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a 256k Storage Disk from ExtraStorage."
		"Why this matters: Stellar Foundry creates many intermediate parts, space resources, and automation outputs. The standard starter disks teach the system; ExtraStorage gives that system headroom once it becomes central to your base."
		"Step by step: Only build high-capacity storage after your physical bulk-storage habits still make sense. Digital capacity is useful, but drawers and dedicated buffers remain valuable."
		"Common mistake: Huge disks do not automatically make poor item routing clean."
	]
	quest.701EC555B9672189.quest_subtitle: "ExtraStorage extends the Refined Storage branch instead of replacing it."
	quest.701EC555B9672189.title: "Plan for high-capacity digital storage"
	quest.7068E428F468E2DB.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Continue into the Venus phase and obtain Neptunium Ingots."
		"Why this matters: Collecting multiple advanced planetary resources lets the pack express a real progression arc rather than one destination with one trophy."
		"Step by step: Store Plutonium, Neptunium, and later advanced resources in a dedicated research or mission-storage area."
		"Common mistake: Dumping rare planetary materials into general bulk storage makes later planning harder."
	]
	quest.7068E428F468E2DB.quest_subtitle: "Build a real off-world material archive."
	quest.7068E428F468E2DB.title: "Bring back Neptunium"
	quest.70E72181A0ECC1A4.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft and place a Starter Energizing Rod."
		"Why this matters: The Rod feeds power into the Energizing Orb. Without a power source and a rod, the Orb cannot complete recipes."
		"Step by step: Place the Rod facing the Orb, then inspect its status. This is your first FE-processing setup."
		"Common mistake: A correctly crafted machine can still do nothing if its facing or energy input is wrong."
	]
	quest.70E72181A0ECC1A4.quest_subtitle: "Processing needs a powered sender."
	quest.70E72181A0ECC1A4.title: "Add the first Energizing Rod"
	quest.710363CE6725A0C3.quest_desc: [
		"Stellar Foundry is a guided technology and space-exploration modpack. The final goal is not simply to craft a rocket, but to build the industrial base that makes repeatable spaceflight possible."
		"The questbook is the main progression tool. Read the descriptions: they explain what to build, why it matters, what to automate next, and which common mistakes to avoid."
		"Main route: survival workshop, Create machines, power, Mekanism, digital storage, pressure systems, launch preparation, off-world industry, planetary colonies."
		"Recommended mindset: progress at a steady pace, finish systems cleanly, and treat every new chapter as a tool for the next one rather than a race to the final rocket."
	]
	quest.710363CE6725A0C3.quest_subtitle: "Read this before you touch the first machine."
	quest.710363CE6725A0C3.title: "Welcome to Stellar Foundry"
	quest.7135EB57CC305D7B.quest_desc: [
		"The final phase of the pack asks you to connect everything you learned: terrestrial factories, advanced power, off-world materials, mission logistics, and useful colonies."
		"There is no single magic trophy that proves a world is well engineered. These quests use concrete items where possible and honest checkmarks where the achievement is architectural."
		"Aim for a world that can support itself and launch again without a painful manual reset."
		"The intended endgame feeling is calm capability: missions can be prepared again, colonies stay useful, and the home factory supports future ambition."
	]
	quest.7135EB57CC305D7B.quest_subtitle: "Stellar Foundry finishes with systems mastery."
	quest.7135EB57CC305D7B.title: "The endgame is a network, not a single item"
	quest.71D902F0B37C522F.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Enrichment Chamber and connect it to your FE grid."
		"Why this matters: This machine supports better material handling and becomes part of efficient ore and resource processing routes."
		"Step by step: Place it near the Infuser, power it, and inspect recipes so you understand what it improves immediately."
		"Common mistake: Do not place machines randomly. A clear processing row makes later automation simple."
	]
	quest.71D902F0B37C522F.quest_subtitle: "Better inputs improve whole factories."
	quest.71D902F0B37C522F.title: "Add the Enrichment Chamber"
	quest.7246FDCBED5EF8C1.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Refined Storage Controller."
		"Why this matters: The Controller represents the network itself. If it is unpowered, attached terminals and drives are just silent boxes."
		"Step by step: Place it near your machine-room power and leave a tidy face or cable path for expansion."
		"Common mistake: A network with no power is not broken. It is simply offline."
	]
	quest.7246FDCBED5EF8C1.quest_subtitle: "Every network needs a powered center."
	quest.7246FDCBED5EF8C1.title: "Build the Controller"
	quest.724BC0E3373029DA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Ender Storage Ender Chest."
		"Why this matters: Unlike a vanilla Ender Chest, this system uses frequency colors so you can build named logistics lanes: launch supplies, colony returns, building blocks, or maintenance parts."
		"Step by step: Craft one chest, decide what that frequency will represent, and resist the temptation to turn every channel into a random dumping ground."
		"Common mistake: A remote chest is only useful when both ends follow the same channel discipline."
	]
	quest.724BC0E3373029DA.quest_subtitle: "Frequency-based item transfer begins here."
	quest.724BC0E3373029DA.title: "Craft an Ender Chest network node"
	quest.725FB67D38AA7200.quest_desc: [
		"The first milestone is a stable surface base with food, storage, basic resource stockpiles, Create rotational power, and enough organization to expand."
		"Do not rush directly toward rockets. Spaceflight becomes fun when your base can replace fuel, parts, and oxygen gear without a long manual grind."
		"The pack will lead you through that foundation step by step."
		"Before leaving this phase, ask whether future-you can find materials quickly, cook safely, and expand machines without demolishing the whole room."
	]
	quest.725FB67D38AA7200.quest_subtitle: "A workshop that can grow into a factory."
	quest.725FB67D38AA7200.title: "Your first serious milestone"
	quest.729BA228C52EE622.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Pressure Chamber Walls and the first Valve."
		"Why this matters: The chamber is a controlled pressure-processing structure. It introduces another major modded-Minecraft skill: building a multiblock that must be complete and correctly formed."
		"Step by step: Gather enough walls for a starter chamber and at least one valve. Check the in-game guide or JEI when assembling it."
		"Common mistake: A chamber that looks box-shaped but lacks the required block layout will not function."
	]
	quest.729BA228C52EE622.quest_subtitle: "Advanced recipes happen in a multiblock."
	quest.729BA228C52EE622.title: "Construct a Pressure Chamber shell"
	quest.72EF2F897DE1E3A8.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Provide a stable power route for the colony."
		"Why this matters: RC3 deliberately gives you more than one valid answer. Flux Networks, Powah remote options, or a thoughtfully designed local generation plan can all work, as long as the colony is not living from a disposable emergency battery forever."
		"Step by step: Use what you learned in the remote logistics chapter and install a solution you can explain and maintain."
		"Common mistake: A machine placed on another world without a long-term power plan is a delayed failure."
	]
	quest.72EF2F897DE1E3A8.quest_subtitle: "Every outpost needs a utility plan."
	quest.72EF2F897DE1E3A8.title: "Add remote power"
	quest.73053F9E31579991.quest_desc: [
		"Construct a launch complex with pad, staging, fuel or supply area, access path, and visual identity. It should look like a location built for spaceflight, not a temporary machine dump."
		"Use blocks and tools from the optional building chapter if they help."
		"A strong launch complex is one of the most memorable things a player can build in this pack."
		"Consider signage, walkways, control rooms, fuel lines, and observation angles. A good launch complex tells the story of its own operation."
	]
	quest.73053F9E31579991.quest_subtitle: "The rocket deserves a home."
	quest.73053F9E31579991.title: "Build a visually coherent launch complex"
	quest.73271CC945A4CF7D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Mechanical Press and prepare it for use."
		"Why this matters: The press is one of the earliest real processing machines. Many components rely on plates, and presses later integrate elegantly with belts."
		"Step by step: Place the press above a Depot first. Power it from your rotation line and process at least one compatible item."
		"Common mistake: The press needs its target in the correct block space beneath it."
	]
	quest.73271CC945A4CF7D.quest_subtitle: "Metal plates begin here."
	quest.73271CC945A4CF7D.title: "Build the Mechanical Press"
	quest.73E5C516382DB2CC.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Modular Router."
		"Why this matters: Routers are powerful when a job is specific: pull from here, send there, filter this, repeat. They reward precise intent."
		"Step by step: Place a Router near a small machine setup and inspect the available modules before automating anything complex."
		"Common mistake: Using a Router without understanding the modules can create invisible item loss or accidental loops."
	]
	quest.73E5C516382DB2CC.quest_subtitle: "One block can solve targeted transport jobs."
	quest.73E5C516382DB2CC.title: "Meet Modular Routers"
	quest.7472493B71BB6460.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the base frame used by several Industrial Foregoing machines."
		"Why this matters: The frame is a planning ingredient. If you understand it early, later machine recipes feel far less random."
		"Step by step: Craft one and inspect the recipes that use it before choosing your first machine direction."
		"Common mistake: Crafting a machine without checking adjacent machines often misses a much better automation route."
	]
	quest.7472493B71BB6460.quest_subtitle: "The first structural component."
	quest.7472493B71BB6460.title: "Craft the Pity Machine Frame"
	quest.74FC609691C31D44.quest_desc: [
		"Immersive Engineering is not the central progression route of Stellar Foundry, but it adds beautiful, grounded, industrial machinery and infrastructure."
		"This chapter is ideal if you enjoy visible machines, multiblocks, conveyor-like factory feeling, and a more analogue complement to high-tech systems."
		"Use it as a deliberate branch, not as a distraction from the space program."
		"Its value here is not speed alone. Immersive Engineering adds place-making: factories that look heavy, visible, and intentionally industrial."
	]
	quest.74FC609691C31D44.quest_subtitle: "Immersive Engineering adds physicality to the factory."
	quest.74FC609691C31D44.title: "Optional: heavy industry aesthetics and multiblocks"
	quest.753AB64D64C80304.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Coke Oven Bricks."
		"Why this matters: This structure teaches the Immersive Engineering building pattern in a gentle way. It is simple enough to verify and useful enough to matter."
		"Step by step: Craft enough bricks for the intended structure, check the manual, and plan a small outdoor industrial corner if desired."
		"Common mistake: Do not assume every multiblock is a single block recipe. Placement order and shape matter."
	]
	quest.753AB64D64C80304.quest_subtitle: "Multiblock learning starts with a classic."
	quest.753AB64D64C80304.title: "Prepare Coke Oven bricks"
	quest.757B64F00BBB63BD.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft External Storage and connect a bulk inventory or drawer system."
		"Why this matters: Huge stacks of common materials are often better kept in visible bulk storage while still being accessible from the digital network."
		"Step by step: Attach External Storage to a sensible target and check how it appears in the Grid."
		"Common mistake: Dumping every cobblestone stack onto tiny disks wastes capacity and hides useful inventory structure."
	]
	quest.757B64F00BBB63BD.quest_subtitle: "Digital access does not require digital capacity for everything."
	quest.757B64F00BBB63BD.title: "External Storage keeps drawers relevant"
	quest.7580FCD8F470EC50.quest_desc: [
		"The main progression ends with the Stellar Foundry Charter. The mastery chapter is not required for release readiness, rockets, or deeper planets."
		"It exists for players who love optimization, megaprojects, and turning a good factory into a memorable one."
		"Use these as self-directed endgame prompts."
		"Pick the goals that inspire you and ignore the rest until they sound fun. Mastery content should extend a world, not turn into a chore list."
	]
	quest.7580FCD8F470EC50.quest_subtitle: "These goals are for players who want the world to keep growing."
	quest.7580FCD8F470EC50.title: "Optional mastery challenges"
	quest.758F4719A8AD03DC.quest_desc: [
		"Your first off-world mission proves that the pack works. The next phase asks whether your factory can support repeated missions, larger builds, and richer processing."
		"Mekanism becomes the backbone of that expansion. This chapter upgrades circuits, material flow, and chemical thinking without immediately jumping to endgame everything."
		"Stay organized. Scaling a messy factory magnifies every earlier problem."
		"Refined Storage - Mekanism Integration supports chemical storage and planning, giving the Mekanism route a cleaner bridge into the main digital-storage philosophy."
	]
	quest.758F4719A8AD03DC.quest_subtitle: "Advanced spaceflight needs advanced industry."
	quest.758F4719A8AD03DC.title: "Scale beyond the starter workshop"
	quest.75B8B0FFE565A216.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Reach the Mars phase of Stellaris progression and return with Plutonium Ingots."
		"Why this matters: Deeper destinations should matter because they provide resources your home world cannot. New materials are the bridge between exploration and advanced crafting."
		"Step by step: Bring back a useful sample and inspect its JEI uses immediately."
		"Common mistake: A rare material that never enters your planning is just sightseeing loot."
	]
	quest.75B8B0FFE565A216.quest_subtitle: "Planetary metals signal new industrial tiers."
	quest.75B8B0FFE565A216.title: "Bring back Plutonium"
	quest.75EA478FB618367A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a MEGA Pattern Provider."
		"Why this matters: The optional AE2 route should not stop at storage. MEGA’s pattern provider gives processing automation more room and makes the expert network feel like a complete alternative specialty."
		"Step by step: Reserve it for a real processing area rather than dropping it randomly next to unrelated machines."
		"Common mistake: High-capacity pattern handling still needs clean machine interfaces and sensible recipe grouping."
	]
	quest.75EA478FB618367A.quest_subtitle: "AE2 automation deserves an equally serious pattern hub."
	quest.75EA478FB618367A.title: "Use a MEGA Pattern Provider"
	quest.768155C16E7C14BB.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the habit of reading the next two or three quests before committing resources."
		"Why this matters: Many machines become far more useful when paired with a second block, a transport method, or a later upgrade. Planning prevents waste."
		"Step by step: Before you mass-craft a component, scan the upcoming quests and identify whether the pack expects you to automate it soon."
		"Common mistake: Rushing one recipe at a time can create dead-end manual setups."
	]
	quest.768155C16E7C14BB.quest_subtitle: "The description often saves resources."
	quest.768155C16E7C14BB.title: "Read quests before crafting"
	quest.773041146EFBF24B.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Mechanical Electrolyzer."
		"Why this matters: This block ties Create’s mechanical logic to gas and fluid preparation. It is a great thematic bridge between early factory work and space operations."
		"Step by step: Place it where basins, shafts, and fluid handling can remain accessible."
		"Common mistake: Forgetting that this addon still expects Create-style machine placement causes many non-working setups."
	]
	quest.773041146EFBF24B.quest_subtitle: "Chemistry meets rotation."
	quest.773041146EFBF24B.title: "Build a Mechanical Electrolyzer"
	quest.77DB6E7C3C6CD784.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Upgrade your mobile inventory at least once."
		"Why this matters: Larger builds and mining trips become more pleasant when you carry more than the bare minimum. This is quality of life, not power creep."
		"Step by step: Craft an Iron Backpack when resources allow. Keep tools, repair items, spare food, and building materials in sensible slots."
		"Common mistake: Do not throw important progression items into random backpack slots without sorting."
	]
	quest.77DB6E7C3C6CD784.quest_subtitle: "Mobile storage should grow with your projects."
	quest.77DB6E7C3C6CD784.title: "Add a backpack upgrade path"
	quest.78100D3D79794991.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Digital Miner."
		"Why this matters: Large projects require dependable material acquisition. The Digital Miner is a clear high-tier milestone in resource automation and planning."
		"Step by step: Before deploying it, inspect its configuration philosophy and think about where it belongs in your world."
		"Common mistake: A powerful machine used without filters or planning can create clutter instead of security."
	]
	quest.78100D3D79794991.quest_subtitle: "Late-game resource security matters."
	quest.78100D3D79794991.title: "Build a Digital Miner"
	quest.78FCB063516DFCC6.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Ender Cell and Ender Gate."
		"Why this matters: As bases spread out, remote machines and launch areas benefit from controlled long-distance energy access. This is a quality-of-life and infrastructure step."
		"Step by step: Craft both blocks, then decide where remote power actually improves your layout."
		"Common mistake: Wireless convenience should simplify the base, not conceal an unstable core grid."
	]
	quest.78FCB063516DFCC6.quest_subtitle: "Ender Cell and Ender Gate extend reach."
	quest.78FCB063516DFCC6.title: "Prepare wireless or remote power logic"
	quest.795D7D620E53DF2B.quest_desc: [
		"PneumaticCraft introduces compressed air, pressure limits, tubing, and machine networks that behave differently from FE cables."
		"This chapter is deliberately placed before the space program. It teaches sealed systems, pressure awareness, and high-tech components that fit the pack theme perfectly."
		"Treat pressure as a real operating condition. More is not always safer."
		"Read gauges and compare production with consumption. Pressure networks become beginner-friendly once you stop guessing and start observing."
	]
	quest.795D7D620E53DF2B.quest_subtitle: "PneumaticCraft teaches gas-like infrastructure early."
	quest.795D7D620E53DF2B.title: "Why pressure matters before space"
	quest.796B99AFA5B66C1D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Oxygen Distributor for off-world support."
		"Why this matters: Personal gear keeps you alive during an expedition. Infrastructure lets you stay, work, and build. This is the beginning of colony thinking."
		"Step by step: Craft the distributor and study how it should be supported before you place it carelessly on another world."
		"Common mistake: Permanent base blocks without a support plan become stranded expensive decorations."
	]
	quest.796B99AFA5B66C1D.quest_subtitle: "The seed of a real outpost."
	quest.796B99AFA5B66C1D.title: "Prepare an Oxygen Distributor"
	quest.79742E4AF13A041A.quest_desc: [
		"This tier completes when launch preparation, fuel stability, the first rocket, and the first off-world expedition are all documented through their patches."
		"Why this matters: Stellar Foundry is not finished when a rocket is crafted. Spaceflight should feel like a earned operational capability."
		"Reward: a spaceflight seal, XP, and a deposit upgrade that reduces base-return friction during longer missions. Its Field Protocol is built for exploratory mobility."
		"The reward supports longer expeditions, but the real achievement is operational readiness: spaceflight has become a repeatable system."
	]
	quest.79742E4AF13A041A.quest_subtitle: "The space program becomes repeatable."
	quest.79742E4AF13A041A.title: "Milestone Tier III: Spaceflight"
	quest.79E7ABE6ADEA40A1.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Formulaic Assemblicator."
		"Why this matters: This machine represents another form of recipe automation and complements the digital-network approach. Different systems solve different production problems."
		"Step by step: Place it where you can compare its role against Refined Storage autocrafting and Create-style assembly."
		"Common mistake: The best endgame base chooses tools intentionally instead of declaring one automation method universally superior."
	]
	quest.79E7ABE6ADEA40A1.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism contributes to high-volume crafting."
	quest.79E7ABE6ADEA40A1.title: "Build a Formulaic Assemblicator"
	quest.7A52D089D60D6277.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Understand how this pack guides you."
		"Why this matters: Several chapters are linear on purpose. They introduce one concept at a time so new players are never forced to guess what to do next."
		"Step by step: Follow the numbered chapters for the main route. Optional chapters are clearly labeled and can be explored when you feel comfortable."
		"Common mistake: Skipping text will make difficult mods feel much harder than they actually are."
	]
	quest.7A52D089D60D6277.quest_subtitle: "This book is a tutorial, roadmap, and checklist."
	quest.7A52D089D60D6277.title: "How to use the questbook"
	quest.7AEF1298B1D3AA9A.quest_desc: [
		"Build one production chain where three or more technology systems cooperate naturally. Example structure: Create handles early shaping, Mekanism handles advanced material transformation, and Refined Storage or Routers handles request and return flow."
		"The exact chain is your design. It should solve a real repeated job."
		"This is an engineering challenge, not a checklist of random adjacent machines."
		"Coherence matters more than mod count. The strongest chain uses multiple systems because each one solves a different part cleanly."
	]
	quest.7AEF1298B1D3AA9A.quest_subtitle: "Integration should be purposeful."
	quest.7AEF1298B1D3AA9A.title: "Use at least three tech mods in one coherent chain"
	quest.7CFA6BD53F78E588.quest_desc: [
		"Create machines are powered by rotation, not Forge Energy. The three concepts you need are speed, stress capacity, and stress impact."
		"Speed controls how quickly machines work. Stress capacity is the power available. Stress impact is how much each machine consumes."
		"When a network stops, use goggles or tooltips to ask whether it is overstressed, too slow, or not connected."
		"When a Create block still feels unclear, use its Ponder scene: hover it in an inventory and hold the Ponder key to open the in-game animated explanation."
	]
	quest.7CFA6BD53F78E588.quest_subtitle: "Rotational power replaces cables here."
	quest.7CFA6BD53F78E588.title: "Meet Create"
	quest.7D12A302DAE31A75.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Pack a serious construction and survival loadout."
		"Why this matters: Off-world building is easier when you bring walls, light, machines, spare tools, storage, and environmental support in a controlled kit."
		"Step by step: Use a higher-tier backpack or a clearly labeled storage crate system for the colony kit."
		"Common mistake: Repeated emergency return trips are usually a packing problem."
	]
	quest.7D12A302DAE31A75.quest_subtitle: "Good colonies are prepared on Earth."
	quest.7D12A302DAE31A75.title: "Stage colony materials at home"
	quest.7D8D1D09719AF4CA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Refined Obsidian Paxel from Mekanism Tools."
		"Why this matters: RC3 adds the official Mekanism Tools addon so advanced materials are not only machine ingredients. They also become practical expedition gear for mining, building, and long off-world sessions."
		"Step by step: Treat this as a durable field tool milestone after your refined material chain is stable."
		"Common mistake: Chasing the tool before the material line is comfortable makes the reward feel like a tax instead of a payoff."
	]
	quest.7D8D1D09719AF4CA.quest_subtitle: "Mekanism Tools now matters to the space-program loop."
	quest.7D8D1D09719AF4CA.title: "Convert Mekanism materials into field equipment"
	quest.7F04354F5EF7F345.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft the Big Rocket Upgrade."
		"Why this matters: Higher travel ambitions should visibly demand a stronger vehicle. This item marks the transition from first-flight capability to broader exploration."
		"Step by step: Check JEI, gather the prerequisites, and craft the upgrade before choosing a deeper mission route."
		"Common mistake: Do not plan a deep-space trip around a vehicle you have not actually upgraded."
	]
	quest.7F04354F5EF7F345.quest_subtitle: "The vehicle grows with the program."
	quest.7F04354F5EF7F345.title: "Prepare a Big Rocket Upgrade"
	quest.7F2CED7F1AF306B6.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Build the first food-preparation block."
		"Why this matters: The Cutting Board introduces food processing without asking you to redesign your entire base. It is a small quality-of-life step that fits early and midgame equally well."
		"Step by step: Craft it and place it in a kitchen or utility corner rather than leaving it lost among machines."
		"Common mistake: Treating food blocks as random clutter makes them much less enjoyable to use."
	]
	quest.7F2CED7F1AF306B6.quest_subtitle: "Farmer’s Delight starts with preparation."
	quest.7F2CED7F1AF306B6.title: "Craft a Cutting Board"
	quest.7D06AFA4D47BE1FF.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Create: New Age Basic Motor."
		"Why this matters: New Age gives the Create branch its own progressive electrical identity instead of only borrowing external FE machinery."
		"Treat it as a parallel engineering path."
		"Place it beside other Create motion options at least once and compare the design language before committing to a larger New Age workshop."
		"Parallel routes are easier to appreciate when you can see why one motor or generator belongs in a specific build."
	]
	quest.7D06AFA4D47BE1FF.quest_subtitle: "Create now has another internal route to motion."
	quest.7D06AFA4D47BE1FF.title: "Introduce a New Age Basic Motor"
	quest.75D725B5E975C591.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Single Battery."
		"Why this matters: Portable charge reduces friction while testing optional machines and utility tools away from your permanent energy grid."
		"It is a convenience tool, not a reason to abandon proper infrastructure."
		"Charge it and spend it at least once before moving on. Portable power makes more sense after you feel the exact quality-of-life gain."
		"It is especially useful during field tests, temporary builds, or side-room setup where the permanent grid is intentionally absent."
	]
	quest.75D725B5E975C591.quest_subtitle: "Portable energy is quality of life, not a grid replacement."
	quest.75D725B5E975C591.title: "Carry a reusable battery"
	quest.6AF08EE19C693185.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Rolling Mill."
		"Why this matters: The Rolling Mill introduces the component-processing rhythm behind wires and connectors in Create Crafts and Additions."
		"Place it close to your Create metal-processing area."
		"Feed it from a clear Create line or keep it beside the metal-processing area so its role in component preparation remains obvious."
		"This block is a gateway into the chapter's electrical parts rather than a one-off machine with no workshop context."
	]
	quest.6AF08EE19C693185.quest_subtitle: "One machine opens a cleaner electrical component chain."
	quest.6AF08EE19C693185.title: "Build a Rolling Mill"
	quest.6F1BA91E18584F73.quest_desc: [
		"Create Crafts and Additions and Create: New Age extend the Create side of Stellar Foundry into wires, motors, generators, and advanced electrical builds."
		"This chapter is optional, but it gives Create-focused players a satisfying engineering bridge between rotational machines and power systems."
		"Use it to build a coherent electrical workshop rather than scattering parts across the factory."
		"Use this branch to link moving shafts, component production, and electrical ideas into one workshop that visibly explains the conversion between systems."
		"It is ideal for players who want the Create side of the pack to remain relevant even while FE infrastructure grows."
	]
	quest.6F1BA91E18584F73.quest_subtitle: "Rotational engineering gains an electrical vocabulary."
	quest.6F1BA91E18584F73.title: "Optional: mechanical motion becomes electricity"
	quest.009DA784B4DC4E22.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Inferium Farmland."
		"Why this matters: Dedicated farmland makes the cultivation branch feel intentional and creates a clear home for your early resource crops."
		"Keep farm tiers visually distinct if you later expand."
		"Start with a modest field and expand after the layout feels readable. Resource farming scales best from a clean prototype."
		"Distinct plots, clear walking paths, and predictable collection points make later automation much easier."
	]
	quest.009DA784B4DC4E22.quest_subtitle: "A resource farm should look like a system, not an accident."
	quest.009DA784B4DC4E22.title: "Prepare Inferium Farmland"
	quest.12BD7C8771701E29.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Energy Laser Relay."
		"Why this matters: Relays are a visually clean way to think about remote energy links and optional-room power layouts."
		"Use them deliberately so their network stays understandable."
		"Label or visually separate relay routes if the room grows. Invisible-looking power still benefits from visible design logic."
		"Do not hide every connection immediately. First make the network understandable; compactness can come after confidence."
	]
	quest.12BD7C8771701E29.quest_subtitle: "Invisible-looking links still deserve clear planning."
	quest.12BD7C8771701E29.title: "Route power with Laser Relays"
	quest.5478F14960018F9E.quest_desc: [
		"Mystical Agriculture and Mystical Agradditions form an optional resource-cultivation route, while Mob Grinding Utils closes practical loops around drops and XP."
		"This branch does not replace factory automation. It rewards players who enjoy building renewable side systems alongside the main industrial arc."
		"Scale it only after the base can support the setup cleanly."
		"Use this path to turn slow resource chores into long-term agricultural infrastructure while keeping the main technology progression meaningful."
		"It complements mining, processing, and factories rather than replacing the rest of the pack with one passive field."
	]
	quest.5478F14960018F9E.quest_subtitle: "Renewable inputs belong beside automation, not instead of it."
	quest.5478F14960018F9E.title: "Optional: cultivate production instead of only mining it"
	quest.5BF2244271E010C7.quest_desc: [
		"Actually Additions adds a compact side-route for conversion, wireless-looking logistics, local power handling, and empowered materials."
		"This branch is optional for the main space route, but it gives builders and automation-minded players several flexible midgame tools."
		"Treat it as a focused engineering lab rather than a replacement for the core factory."
		"Use this chapter when you want a focused side laboratory with item conversion, compact utility, wireless-looking power routing, and playful remote interfaces."
		"Keep the lab compact, labeled, and visually distinct from the main factory so the branch feels like an intentional research wing."
	]
	quest.5BF2244271E010C7.quest_subtitle: "A compact side laboratory for clever utility systems."
	quest.5BF2244271E010C7.title: "Optional: reconstruction engineering"
	quest.4488BA11E4E18029.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft Basic Reactor Casing."
		"Why this matters: Casings turn the idea of a reactor into a physical multiblock project and define the first construction milestone."
		"Stage more than one casing if you intend to build immediately."
		"Lay out the intended footprint before crafting too many casings. Large multiblocks are easier to correct before the walls rise."
		"Reactor mistakes are cheap on paper and expensive once every side has been enclosed."
	]
	quest.4488BA11E4E18029.quest_subtitle: "The shell comes before the system."
	quest.4488BA11E4E18029.title: "Craft Basic Reactor Casing"
	quest.0D9F562D691DAE53.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Generator Coil."
		"Why this matters: Coils move the New Age route from simple parts toward purposeful electrical apparatus and larger machines."
		"Keep them near the future assembly footprint."
		"Keep coils in small batch production if the route interests you. Advanced electrical branches feel better when subcomponents stop being surprise chores."
		"They foreshadow larger machines, so this is a good moment to decide where the electrical workshop can expand."
	]
	quest.0D9F562D691DAE53.quest_subtitle: "Advanced power builds need recognizable subcomponents."
	quest.0D9F562D691DAE53.title: "Prepare a Generator Coil"
	quest.250C5145E2E49C1A.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Electric Motor."
		"Why this matters: Motors invert the relationship and let electrical systems re-enter the Create machine line when that is more convenient."
		"This makes hybrid workshops possible."
		"Use it for targeted motion where FE-to-rotation conversion solves a layout problem cleanly, not as a replacement for every water wheel or windmill."
		"The point is conversion control: choose the energy direction that makes the surrounding machine line more elegant."
	]
	quest.250C5145E2E49C1A.quest_subtitle: "The bridge works in both directions."
	quest.250C5145E2E49C1A.title: "Drive motion with an Electric Motor"
	quest.5CDFF09AD80CB238.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Obtain Inferium Essence."
		"Why this matters: Essence tiers define the long-term pacing of Mystical Agriculture. Inferium is the first visible proof that the route is available."
		"Store it neatly; later conversions become easier to understand when the tiers stay separated."
		"Make sure you understand that essence tiers are a ladder. Early Inferium is the beginning of a system, not a dead-end drop."
		"Clear early farm organization prevents tedious rework once fields, accelerators, and crafting stations become more serious."
	]
	quest.5CDFF09AD80CB238.quest_subtitle: "The first essence tier anchors the whole branch."
	quest.5CDFF09AD80CB238.title: "Gather Inferium"
	quest.75D2F70C94503C3D.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Obtain a Yellorium Ingot."
		"Why this matters: This is the basic fuel-adjacent resource that tells you the optional reactor route is materially available."
		"Do not scale reactor plans before the underlying resource supply is clear."
		"Track how much of this resource you can actually supply before designing something massive. Fuel confidence should guide reactor scale."
		"Reliable input matters more than a dramatic shell that spends most of its time starved."
	]
	quest.75D2F70C94503C3D.quest_subtitle: "Reactor ambitions need a reliable material basis."
	quest.75D2F70C94503C3D.title: "Acquire Yellorium"
	quest.02B1435380885607.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Passive FE Power Tap."
		"Why this matters: A reactor is only useful when its output enters a power system you can read and measure."
		"Connect output through sensible buffers instead of directly into a chaotic machine wall."
		"Test output through a buffer or visible grid point before wiring the entire base directly. Measurement should precede confidence."
		"That single buffer gives you a readable signal when generation, transfer, or demand becomes the real limiting factor."
	]
	quest.02B1435380885607.quest_subtitle: "Generation only matters once it joins the grid."
	quest.02B1435380885607.title: "Export power with a Power Tap"
	quest.4A265E2D19C04E5E.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Infusion Altar."
		"Why this matters: The altar establishes the crafting station for seeds and advanced cultivation progression."
		"Place it where the required pedestals and storage can remain tidy."
		"Leave room around the altar and plan storage nearby. Ritual-like crafting becomes beginner-friendly when the work area announces how it is used."
		"The visual layout teaches the recipe flow before you ever need to memorize it."
	]
	quest.4A265E2D19C04E5E.quest_subtitle: "A dedicated station keeps cultivation readable."
	quest.4A265E2D19C04E5E.title: "Build the Infusion Altar"
	quest.5A5D7E4B68A77957.quest_desc: [
		"Extreme Reactors is treated here as an optional alternative power-engineering route, not as the mandatory energy path of Stellar Foundry."
		"Use this chapter when you want a contained multiblock project with clear machine-room identity and later turbine ambitions."
		"Keep reactor construction deliberate, readable, and separate from your first-power grid."
		"Use this branch after your first FE grid feels understood, so the reactor becomes a deliberate expansion rather than a substitute for learning basics."
		"A reactor plant should be a planned room with service access, readable fuel handling, and a visible relationship to the wider power system."
	]
	quest.5A5D7E4B68A77957.quest_subtitle: "A parallel energy project for players who want it."
	quest.5A5D7E4B68A77957.title: "Optional: large-scale reactor engineering"
	quest.66C9ED08933C5B67.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Absorption Hopper."
		"Why this matters: Mob Grinding Utils helps side farms and drop rooms stay clean without hand-collecting items and XP."
		"This is a utility bridge between renewable mob output and organized storage."
		"Pair collection with visible item storage so you can tell whether the farm is producing, stalling, or overflowing at a glance."
		"A farm that collects itself becomes a real system instead of a field that still waits for the player every few minutes."
	]
	quest.66C9ED08933C5B67.quest_subtitle: "Drops become infrastructure when they collect themselves."
	quest.66C9ED08933C5B67.title: "Collect drops with an Absorption Hopper"
	quest.157CC02C2BFB7E67.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an XP Solidifier."
		"Why this matters: XP becomes a manageable byproduct instead of background clutter once it has a dedicated processing point."
		"Keep XP handling near the mob system that produces it."
		"Decide whether XP is stored, converted, or consumed locally. Treat it like any other output stream with a purpose."
		"Good farm design respects experience as a resource, not as visual noise left around the machine room."
	]
	quest.157CC02C2BFB7E67.quest_subtitle: "A good farm handles experience as deliberately as items."
	quest.157CC02C2BFB7E67.title: "Solidify XP as a usable output"
	quest.54EACBD076E4D3E1.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Obtain Insanium Essence."
		"Why this matters: Agradditions gives the optional cultivation branch a visible high-end destination rather than leaving it as only early utility."
		"Claim the patch once the route feels genuinely established."
		"Use this as a capstone that proves the branch can sustain long-term resource ambition without losing its structure."
		"The advanced essence tier is meaningful because the earlier altar, crystals, farmland, and collection logic now support it."
	]
	quest.54EACBD076E4D3E1.quest_subtitle: "The branch ends with a clear advanced resource tier."
	quest.54EACBD076E4D3E1.title: "Reach Agradditions-level essence"
	quest.5EC9A125437229E7.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Obtain a Prosperity Shard."
		"Why this matters: Prosperity materials are the structural foundation for seed crafting and mark the start of the cultivation branch."
		"Treat the first shard as a planning signal, not a demand to rush every seed type."
		"Store Prosperity materials with the rest of the cultivation ingredients so the chapter develops its own visible resource shelf."
		"That small organization habit makes later seed work calmer because the foundation items stay easy to find."
	]
	quest.5EC9A125437229E7.quest_subtitle: "A resource route begins with its foundation material."
	quest.5EC9A125437229E7.title: "Find the prosperity basis"
	quest.6E74643639AF49AA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Heater."
		"Why this matters: The Heater makes New Age feel like a broader applied-engineering system rather than only motors and cables."
		"It belongs in an intentionally planned utility bay."
		"Use the Heater as an example of utility blocks that make a workshop feel specialized rather than generic."
		"Specialization gives optional branches identity: the room should begin to look like it exists for applied electrical engineering."
	]
	quest.6E74643639AF49AA.quest_subtitle: "A good workshop gains specialized utility blocks."
	quest.6E74643639AF49AA.title: "Build a Heater"
	quest.591B98E4BD47B9CA.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft an Inferium Growth Accelerator."
		"Why this matters: Growth accelerators reward players who invest in infrastructure rather than simply making larger fields."
		"Use a small test plot first so the layout remains transparent."
		"Test a small before-and-after patch so the improvement is visible rather than assumed. Infrastructure upgrades should teach you what they change."
		"Speed upgrades are most satisfying when you can connect the output increase to a deliberate design choice."
	]
	quest.591B98E4BD47B9CA.quest_subtitle: "Speed is best when the structure stays understandable."
	quest.591B98E4BD47B9CA.title: "Accelerate growth responsibly"
	quest.6DC7BFEFDA1FD7A1.quest_desc: [
		"Goal: Craft a Basic Reactor Control Rod."
		"Why this matters: Control components remind you that this route is about managed output, not merely placing fuel blocks and hoping."
		"A reactor room should look operable, not accidental."
		"Read control adjustments as tuning rather than decoration. Reactor components should change how confidently you operate the system."
		"This branch rewards measured operation: understand the machine first, then optimize it."
	]
	quest.6DC7BFEFDA1FD7A1.quest_subtitle: "Output is stronger when it can be shaped."
	quest.6DC7BFEFDA1FD7A1.title: "Control the chain with Control Rods"
